{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FFM6WwBtpht95fLwUBzzXN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Area 12: Gate and `ignore`\n2\t\n3\t## 1. Purpose\n4\t\n5\tThe **gate** is the pre-commit hook that runs a quick review of exactly the\n6\tstaged content of a commit and fails open: only a finding at or above the\n7\tconfigured severity blocks the commit; every operational failure prints a\n8\twarning and lets the commit through.\n9\t\n10\tThis area owns:\n11\t\n12\t- the hook script (`pre-commit.sh`, shipped unchanged from Go) and its\n13\t  contract with the CLI;\n14\t- installing, refreshing, inspecting, and removing the hook in a repository\n15\t  (`roast gate enable|disable|status`), including coexistence with a\n16\t  **foreign** (someone else's) pre-commit hook and with a shared\n17\t  `core.hooksPath` dispatcher;\n18\t- the per-repository enrollment decision stored in local Git config;\n19\t- the hidden `roast gate settings` query the hook makes;\n20\t- the **review-time bootstrap**: the one-time offer, made before a review\n21\t  runs, to enable the gate;\n22\t- `roast ignore` (and the helper `init` reuses), which adds `/.roast/` to\n23\t  the toplevel `.gitignore` so run records are not committed.\n24\t\n25\tThe gate reads only a project config at the Git toplevel, because the hook\n26\truns from the toplevel without `--config`.\n27\t\n28\t## 2. Behavior contract\n29\t\n30\t### 2.1 Constants\n31\t\n32\t| Name | Value |\n33\t|------|-------|\n34\t| hook name | `pre-commit` |\n35\t| sidecar name | `roast-pre-commit` |\n36\t| hook marker | `# roast-gate-hook: v1` |\n37\t| hook header | `\"#!/bin/sh\\n# roast-gate-hook: v1\\n\"` |\n38\t| append begin marker | see 2.6 |\n39\t| append end marker | `# <<< roast pre-commit gate <<<` |\n40\t| decision config key | `roast.gate` |\n41\t| notice config key | `roast.gate-notice` (value written: `sent`) |\n42\t| default gate timeout | `180` seconds |\n43\t| default gate severity | `HIGH` |\n44\t| state ignore entry | `/.roast/` (from the run-record state dir `.roast`) |\n45\t\n46\t**Manual line** -- the one line that invokes the sidecar; it is both the\n47\tbody of the appended block and what a user adds by hand to a hook Roast\n48\twill not edit:\n49\t\n50\t```sh\n51\t\"$(git rev-parse --git-path hooks/roast-pre-commit)\" || exit $?\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\t**HookScript** is the byte-exact content of `pre-commit.sh` (it starts with\n55\tthe hook header). Every \"is it current\" check is an exact byte comparison\n56\tagainst it. Because the TS version ships the identical file, hooks\n57\tinstalled by the Go version compare equal and are not reported stale. The\n58\tfile must reach `dist/cli.js` byte-for-byte (esbuild `text` loader; no\n59\treformatting, LF line endings).\n60\t\n61\t### 2.2 Git plumbing\n62\t\n63\tAll Git calls are `git -C <repo> ...` where `<repo>` is the working-tree\n64\troot from `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` (the scope area's `gitRoot`).\n65\t\n66\t- **Hook path resolution** (`resolveHookPath(repo, name)`):\n67\t  `git -C <repo> rev-parse --git-path hooks/<name>`, stdout trimmed. Non-zero\n68\t  exit -> error `resolve hooks path in <repo>: <err>`; empty output -> error\n69\t  `resolve hooks path in <repo>: git returned nothing`. A relative result is\n70\t  joined onto `<repo>`. Git itself honours `core.hooksPath` and, in a linked\n71\t  worktree, the common git dir (hooks are shared across worktrees). Used for\n72\t  both `hooks/pre-commit` (the hook path) and `hooks/roast-pre-commit` (the\n73\t  sidecar path).\n74\t- **Shared** = `git -C <repo> config --get core.hooksPath` exits 0. Note:\n75\t  no `--local`; a global or system `core.hooksPath` also counts.\n76\t- **Config get** (`--local`): `git -C <repo> config --local --get <key>`;\n77\t  any failure reads as `\"\"`; output trimmed.\n78\t- **Config set**: `git -C <repo> config --local <key> <value>`; failure ->\n79\t  error `git config <key>: <err>: <trimmed combined output>`.\n80\t- **Config unset**: `git -C <repo> config --local --unset <key>`; callers\n81\t  ignore its failure (exit 5 means \"not set\").\n82\t\n83\t### 2.3 Enrollment decision\n84\t\n85\t`Decision` is one of `none` (Go `\"\"`), `enabled`, `declined`.\n86\t\n87\t`readDecision`: local `roast.gate`, trimmed and lowercased:\n88\t\n89\t- `enabled | enable | true | yes | on | 1` -> `enabled`\n90\t- `declined | disabled | false | no | off | 0` -> `declined`\n91\t- anything else, including unset -> `none` (a typo means \"unanswered\")\n92\t\n93\tThe hook script accepts exactly the same enabled aliases (it reads with\n94\t`--local`, so a global `roast.gate` never enrolls a repo).\n95\t\n96\t`recordDecision(repo, d)`: first unset `roast.gate-notice` (ignore errors);\n97\tthen if `d` is `none` unset `roast.gate` (ignore errors) and return;\n98\totherwise set `roast.gate` to `enabled` or `declined`.\n99\t\n100\t`recordNotice(repo)`: set `roast.gate-notice` to `sent`.\n101\t\n102\t### 2.4 Inspect (never mutates)\n103\t\n104\t`inspect(repo) -> Status` with fields `repo`, `decision`, `hookPath`,\n105\t`sidecarPath`, `shared`, `exists`, `ours`, `appended`, `foreign`,\n106\t`appendable`, `executable`, `stale`, `noticeSent`. At most one of `ours`,\n107\t`appended`, `foreign` is true.\n108\t\n109\tAlgorithm:\n110\t\n111\t1. Resolve hook path and sidecar path (errors propagate). Set `shared`,\n112\t   `decision`, `noticeSent` (= local `roast.gate-notice` non-empty).\n113\t2. `lstat(hookPath)`. ENOENT -> return (all file flags false). Other error\n114\t   -> `stat <path>: <err>`.\n115\t3. `exists = true`; `executable = (lstat mode & 0o100) != 0` (owner execute\n116\t   bit; Git silently skips a hook without it).\n117\t4. A symlink is `foreign` (never appendable); return.\n118\t5. Read the file (error -> `read <path>: <err>`). Classify:\n119\t   - body starts with the hook header -> `ours`;\n120\t     `stale = body !== HookScript || !executable`.\n121\t   - else if the body contains a valid appended block (2.6) -> `appended`;\n122\t     `stale = !sidecarCurrent(sidecarPath)`. The foreign file's own mode\n123\t     never feeds `stale` (Roast does not repair it); it feeds `active`.\n124\t   - else `foreign`; `appendable = appendable(bodyBytes)`.\n125\t\n126\t`sidecarCurrent(path)`: `stat` (follows symlinks) succeeds, owner execute\n127\tbit set, and content equals HookScript.\n128\t\n129\t`active(status) = decision === enabled && (ours || appended) && executable`.\n130\t\n131\t**Summary** (one line, first match wins; `<p>` is `hookPath`). The Go\n132\tstrings use an em dash (U+2014), and so does the real TS output: the\n133\tcharacter is kept and written as the escape `\\u2014` in TS source (spec.md\n134\tcross-cutting \"Output strings\"). Where this spec writes `--` inside these\n135\tquoted output strings, read it as U+2014; `pre-commit.sh` bytes are\n136\tunchanged:\n137\t\n138\t1. `(ours||appended) && !executable`: `INSTALLED BUT NOT RUNNING -- <p> is\n139\t   not executable, so git skips it (chmod +x it, or ``roast gate enable``\n140\t   for roast's own hook)`\n141\t2. `(ours||appended) && stale`: ``installed dispatcher is stale -- run\n142\t   `roast gate enable` to refresh: <p>``\n143\t3. `(ours||appended) && decision=declined`: `declined for this repo;\n144\t   dispatcher retained: <p>`\n145\t4. `(ours||appended) && decision!=enabled`: ``dispatcher installed but not\n146\t   enrolled in this repo (`roast gate enable` enables it): <p>``\n147\t5. `ours`: `installed: <p>`\n148\t6. `appended`: `installed via an appended block in a foreign hook: <p>`\n149\t7. `foreign && declined`: `declined; a foreign pre-commit hook is present\n150\t   (untouched): <p>`\n151\t8. `foreign && appendable`: ``not installed -- a foreign pre-commit hook is\n152\t   present (untouched); `roast gate enable` appends to it: <p>``\n153\t9. `foreign`: `not installed -- a foreign pre-commit hook is present and is\n154\t   not an appendable shell script (untouched): <p>`\n155\t10. `declined`: ``declined for this repo (`roast gate enable` turns it on)``\n156\t11. `enabled`: ``enabled for this repo but the hook is missing -- run\n157\t    `roast gate enable` to reinstall``\n158\t12. otherwise: ``not enrolled (`roast gate enable` installs it)``\n159\t\n160\tThe doctor area's `git-gate` check consumes `inspect`, `stale`, `active`,\n161\tand `summary` (warn when `stale || (enabled && !active)`).\n162\t\n163\t### 2.5 Appendable foreign hooks\n164\t\n165\t`appendable(bytes)` is deliberately conservative:\n166\t\n167\t1. Empty, or not valid UTF-8 -> false. (Check validity on the raw bytes,\n168\t   e.g. `new TextDecoder('utf-8', {fatal:true})`; do not decode lossily\n169\t   first.)\n170\t2. First line (up to the first `\\n`), strip one trailing `\\r`, trim\n171\t   whitespace. Must start with `#!`, else false.\n172\t3. Split the rest on whitespace; none -> false. `interp = basename(f[0])`.\n173\t4. If `interp === 'env'`: need `f[1]`, else false; `f[1]` starting with\n174\t   `-` or containing `=` -> false; `interp = basename(f[1])`.\n175\t5. True iff `interp` is one of `sh`, `bash`, `dash`, `ksh`, `zsh`.\n176\t\n177\tPinned cases: `#!/bin/sh\\n`, `#!/bin/bash -e\\n`, `#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n`,\n178\t`#!/usr/bin/env zsh\\nx\\n` -> true; `#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n`,\n179\t`#!/usr/bin/perl\\n`, `#!/usr/bin/env -S bash\\n`, `no shebang\\n`, `\"\"`,\n180\t`\"\\x00\\x01binary\"` -> false.\n181\t\n182\t### 2.6 The appended block\n183\t\n184\tMarkers, each a whole line:\n185\t\n186\t```text\n187\t# >>> roast pre-commit gate (managed by `roast gate`) >>>\n188\t# <<< roast pre-commit gate <<<\n189\t```\n190\t\n191\tBlock text inserted (note the leading blank line):\n192\t\n193\t```text\n194\t\n195\t# >>> roast pre-commit gate (managed by `roast gate`) >>>\n196\t# Added by `roast gate enable`. Delete this block (or run\n197\t# `roast gate disable`) to remove the gate; the rest of this file is yours.\n198\t\"$(git rev-parse --git-path hooks/roast-pre-commit)\" || exit $?\n199\t# <<< roast pre-commit gate <<<\n200\t```\n201\t\n202\ti.e. `\"\\n\" + begin + \"\\n\" + comment1 + \"\\n\" + comment2 + \"\\n\" +\n203\tmanualLine + \"\\n\" + end + \"\\n\"`.\n204\t\n205\t**Detection** (`appendedBlock(lines)`, lines = body split on `\\n`): scan\n206\tlines, comparing each trimmed line. A line equal to the begin marker sets\n207\t`start = i` and clears `hasInvocation`. A line equal to the end marker while\n208\t`start >= 0`: if `hasInvocation`, return `[start, i]`; otherwise reset\n209\t`start = -1`. A line equal to the manual line while `start >= 0` sets\n210\t`hasInvocation`. No match -> not found. So: markers alone are not\n211\tauthorship; a begin without an end is not a block; edits to the comment\n212\tlines inside a block keep it recognizable. Ownership is anchored: `ours`\n213\trequires the header at byte 0, never \"contains the marker somewhere\".\n214\t\n215\t**Append** (`appendBlock(path)`): read bytes; mode = current permission\n216\tbits (fallback `0o755` if stat fails) -- preserved exactly, execute bit\n217\tincluded, so a hook the owner `chmod -x`'d stays disabled. Find the first\n218\t`\\n`; none -> the file is a one-line hook with no trailing newline\n219\t(`appendable` accepts it): append a `\\n` to the body first, then proceed\n220\t(deliberate change 19; Go failed here with `append gate to <path>: no\n221\tcomplete shebang line` and `gate enable` exited 4). Write\n222\t`body[..=nl] + block + body[nl+1..]` atomically with that mode. The\n223\tblock goes right after the shebang (not at EOF) because a hook ending in\n224\t`exit 0` or `exec ...` would never reach a tail block. Consequence: Roast\n225\truns first, and a blocking review stops the foreign hook from running.\n226\t\n227\t**Strip** (`stripBlock(path)`): read; keep mode (fallback `0o755`); split on\n228\t`\\n`; no valid block -> error `remove gate from <path>: the roast block has\n229\tno closing marker; left the file untouched (delete the block by hand)`. If\n230\tthe line before `start` is blank (trimmed empty), include it in the removed\n231\trange. Rejoin the remaining lines with `\\n` and write atomically. Every\n232\tother byte is preserved.\n233\t\n234\t### 2.7 Writing files\n235\t\n236\t- **writeFileAtomic(path, body, mode)**: create a temp file in\n237\t  `dirname(path)` named `.<basename>.roast-<random>` with exclusive create\n238\t  (`O_CREAT|O_EXCL`, mode `0o600`, unpredictable name; retry on `EEXIST`),\n239\t  write, `fchmod(mode)`, close, `rename` over `path`; remove the temp file on\n240\t  any failure. Never use a predictable temp name: `core.hooksPath` can point\n241\t  inside the working tree (`.githooks`), where a checked-out symlink at a\n242\t  predictable temp path would redirect the write. Errors: `create temp file\n243\t  for <path>: ...`, `write <tmp>: ...`, `chmod <tmp>: ...`, `close <tmp>:\n244\t  ...`, `replace <path>: ...`.\n245\t- **writeScript(path, body)**: `mkdir -p dirname(path)` (mode `0o755`;\n246\t  error `mkdir <dir>: ...`), then `writeFileAtomic(path, body, 0o755)`.\n247\t- **writeSidecar(path)**: `lstat`; symlink -> error ``<path> is a symlink\n248\t  roast did not create; move it aside and re-run `roast gate enable` ``;\n249\t  exists and content does not start with the hook header -> error\n250\t  ``<path> already exists and was not written by roast; move it aside and\n251\t  re-run `roast gate enable` ``; other stat error -> `stat <path>: ...`.\n252\t  Otherwise `writeScript(path, HookScript)`.\n253\t- **removeOwnedSidecar(path)**: absent -> ok; symlink -> leave; content not\n254\t  starting with the header -> leave; else delete (ENOENT ignored).\n255\t- **refreshOwnedSidecar(path)**: absent -> ok; not a regular file -> leave;\n256\t  starts with header and differs from HookScript -> `writeSidecar(path)`;\n257\t  else nothing. Never creates a sidecar.\n258\t\n259\t### 2.8 Install\n260\t\n261\t`install(repo) -> {action, status}` never records a decision (callers do).\n262\tUses `status = inspect(repo)` (the pre-install status is returned):\n263\t\n264\t| State | Effect | Action |\n265\t|-------|--------|--------|\n266\t| foreign, not appendable | `writeSidecar` only; hook untouched | `manual` |\n267\t| foreign, appendable | `writeSidecar`; `appendBlock(hookPath)` | `appended` |\n268\t| appended, not stale | none | `up-to-date` |\n269\t| appended, stale | `writeSidecar` | `refreshed` |\n270\t| ours, not stale | none | `up-to-date` |\n271\t| ours, stale | `writeScript(hookPath, HookScript)`, fixes mode | `refreshed` |\n272\t| no hook | `writeScript(hookPath, HookScript)` | `installed` |\n273\t\n274\t### 2.9 Remove\n275\t\n276\t`remove(repo) -> {action, status}`:\n277\t\n278\t1. `status = inspect(repo)`.\n279\t2. If `shared`: when `(ours || appended) && stale`, run `install(repo)`\n280\t   (older dispatchers lack the consent check); then\n281\t   `refreshOwnedSidecar(sidecarPath)`; return `preserved`. The shared\n282\t   dispatcher is never deleted.\n283\t3. Otherwise: `ours` -> delete hook (ENOENT ignored; error `remove <path>:\n284\t   ...`), action `removed`; `appended` -> `stripBlock`, action `removed`;\n285\t   else `nothing`.\n286\t4. In every non-shared case, `removeOwnedSidecar(sidecarPath)` (an error\n287\t   here returns the action computed so far plus the error).\n288\t\n289\t### 2.10 Commands\n290\t\n291\tAll gate subcommands take no positional arguments (extra args -> usage\n292\terror, exit 2). `roast gate` with no subcommand prints help, exit 0.\n293\tErrors that are not usage errors exit 4 (the CLI's generic code).\n294\t\n295\t**`roast gate enable`**\n296\t\n297\t1. Git root of cwd; failure -> usage error `not inside a Git repository`.\n298\t2. `gateConfigPath(repo)` = project-config search starting and stopping at\n299\t   the toplevel (only `<toplevel>/.roast.json`, a non-directory). Search\n300\t   error -> usage error with that message. Not found -> usage error:\n301\t   ``the pre-commit gate runs from the Git toplevel and finds no\n302\t   .roast.json there; put the project config at the toplevel (`npx roast\n303\t   init`) before enabling the gate``. The config is not loaded,\n304\t   validated, or trust-checked.\n305\t3. `install(repo)`, then `recordDecision(repo, enabled)` -- also for\n306\t   `manual`.\n307\t4. Output on stdout:\n308\t   - `manual`: ``<hookPath> is not an appendable shell script; Roast left\n309\t     it untouched.\\nAdd this line manually:\\n\\n    <manualLine>\\n`` and\n310\t     stop.\n311\t   - `installed`: `gate installed: <hookPath>`\n312\t   - `appended`: `gate appended to existing hook: <hookPath>`\n313\t   - `refreshed`: `gate refreshed: <hookPath>`\n314\t   - `up-to-date`: `gate already up to date: <hookPath>`\n315\t   - then, for all of the above four: `bypass one commit with: ROAST_SKIP=1\n316\t     git commit ...`\n317\t\n318\t**`roast gate disable`** (no config required)\n319\t\n320\t1. Git root; failure -> usage error `not inside a Git repository`.\n321\t2. `remove(repo)`, then `recordDecision(repo, declined)`.\n322\t3. stdout: `removed` -> `gate removed from <hookPath>`; `preserved` ->\n323\t   `gate disabled for this repository; shared dispatcher preserved at\n324\t   <hookPath>`; otherwise `no Roast gate was installed; recorded the\n325\t   decline`.\n326\t\n327\t**`roast gate status`**\n328\t\n329\t1. Git root; failure -> usage error `not inside a Git repository`.\n330\t2. `inspect(repo)`; print exactly three lines (labels padded to align):\n331\t\n332\t   ```text\n333\t   repo:     <repo>\n334\t   gate:     <summary>\n335\t   decision: <enabled|declined|none recorded>\n336\t   ```\n337\t\n338\t**`roast gate settings`** (hidden from help)\n339\t\n340\t- Flag `--config <path>` (default: nearest `.roast.json` from cwd up to\n341\t  the toplevel, the standard project-config lookup). Loads the config the\n342\t  standard way (all failures are usage errors, exit 2; a missing config\n343\t  names `npx roast init`). No trust check.\n344\t- stdout, exactly: `timeout_seconds=<n>\\nseverity=<SEV>\\n` where `n` is\n345\t  `gate.timeout_seconds` or 180, and `SEV` is `gate.severity` uppercased or\n346\t  `HIGH`. Environment variables never affect these values (the retired\n347\t  `ROAST_GATE_TIMEOUT` / `ROAST_GATE_SEVERITY` are ignored).\n348\t\n349\tConfig validation of the `gate` section belongs to the config area and is\n350\trestated here for completeness: `timeout_seconds` integer >= 0 (0 disables\n351\tthe watchdog); `severity` case-insensitively one of `INFO`, `LOW`,\n352\t`MEDIUM`, `HIGH`, `CRITICAL`; `offer` boolean, unset means true. Invalid\n353\tvalues fail any config load with a usage error (exit 2).\n354\t\n355\t### 2.11 Review-time bootstrap\n356\t\n357\tRuns before the review itself (before trust, scope, or any network) when\n358\tthe invoked command is the bare root command or `review`, and\n359\t`--error-format` is not `json` (`--format json` does not suppress it).\n360\tNothing here can fail the review: all failures are silent or printed as a\n361\twarning.\n362\t\n363\t**Preconditions** (any failing -> do nothing, silently):\n364\t\n365\t1. cwd is in a Git repository (`repo` = toplevel).\n366\t2. `gateConfigPath(repo)` finds `<toplevel>/.roast.json` without error.\n367\t   A config only in a subdirectory never triggers an offer, since the hook\n368\t   could not see it.\n369\t3. That file loads (raw config load; no trust check, no stored\n370\t   credentials). A load error is silent here; the review reports it.\n371\t\n372\t**Options**: `noOffer = gate.offer === false`; a `prompt` function exists\n373\tonly when stdin and stderr are both terminals (use the swappable\n374\t`interactiveTerminals` seam). The prompt writes `<question> [Y/n] ` to\n375\tstderr and reads one line from the one shared stdin reader (the same\n376\treader the rest of the CLI uses, never a fresh buffered reader): `\"\"`,\n377\t`y`, `yes` (case-insensitive,\n378\ttrimmed) -> yes; EOF with no input -> no; anything else -> no. Messages go\n379\tto stderr as `roast: <message>\\n`. If bootstrap returns an error, print\n380\t`roast: pre-commit gate setup skipped: <err>` to stderr and continue.\n381\t\n382\t**Algorithm** (`bootstrap`, returns an outcome: `quiet`, `suppressed`,\n383\t`satisfied`, `installed`, `refreshed`, `declined`, `hinted`):\n384\t\n385\t1. If `noOffer`, or env `GIT_INDEX_FILE` is non-empty (we are inside a Git\n386\t   hook, e.g. the gate's own review), or `repo` is empty -> `suppressed`.\n387\t   `ROAST_NO_HOOK` has no effect.\n388\t2. `status = inspect(repo)`.\n389\t3. If `shared`: `refreshOwnedSidecar(sidecarPath)`.\n390\t4. If `decision !== enabled && (ours || appended) && stale`: `install(repo)`\n391\t   (refreshes only a recognized Roast dispatcher, never a foreign hook, so\n392\t   an inherited old shared dispatcher gains the consent check), then\n393\t   re-`inspect`.\n394\t5. `declined` -> `quiet`.\n395\t6. `enabled` -> `satisfied` if `active && !stale`; otherwise run the\n396\t   install step below without recording.\n397\t7. (decision `none`) If `foreign && !appendable` -> hint: ``this repo's\n398\t   pre-commit hook is not an appendable shell script, so Roast left it\n399\t   untouched; run `roast gate enable` to install the sidecar and print the\n400\t   line to add``.\n401\t8. No `prompt` -> hint: ``no pre-commit gate in this repo; run `roast gate\n402\t   enable` to install it (non-interactive runs never install Git hooks\n403\t   without consent)``.\n404\t9. Ask: `Install the Roast pre-commit gate in this repository (<repo>)?`,\n405\t   or when `foreign`: `This repository already has a pre-commit hook.\n406\t   Append the Roast gate to it (<hookPath>)?`. Prompt error -> return it.\n407\t10. No -> `recordDecision(declined)`; print ``gate declined for this\n408\t    repository; `roast gate enable` turns it on later``; `declined`.\n409\t11. Yes -> install step with recording.\n410\t\n411\t**Install step** (`record` flag): `install(repo)`.\n412\t\n413\t- `manual`: if `record`, `recordDecision(enabled)`; then hint: ``this\n414\t  repo's pre-commit hook cannot be appended to, so Roast left it untouched;\n415\t  add this line to enable the gate:\\n    <manualLine>``.\n416\t- otherwise, if `record`, `recordDecision(enabled)`; then `installed` ->\n417\t  print `pre-commit gate installed: <hookPath> (bypass one commit with\n418\t  ROAST_SKIP=1)`, outcome `installed`; `appended` -> print `pre-commit gate\n419\t  appended to the existing hook: <hookPath>`, outcome `installed`;\n420\t  `refreshed` -> outcome `refreshed` (silent); else `satisfied`.\n421\t\n422\t**Hint** (this is \"the gate hint printed during review\"): if\n423\t`noticeSent`, return `quiet` without printing. Otherwise print the message,\n424\t`recordNotice(repo)`, return `hinted` (a `recordNotice` failure is returned\n425\tas the error). A hint is printed at most once per repository until a\n426\tdecision is recorded (recording a decision clears the notice). A\n427\tsuppressed offer (`gate.offer: false`) does not consume the notice.\n428\t\n429\tThe CLI messages here say bare `roast` (not `npx roast`); that is a code\n430\tstring, kept as is.\n431\t\n432\t### 2.12 Hook script contract (`pre-commit.sh`, shipped unchanged)\n433\t\n434\tInstalled as the hook (mode `0o755`) or as the sidecar. Interface:\n435\t\n436\t- **Inputs**: Git's hook environment, above all `GIT_INDEX_FILE` (the\n437\t  temporary index holding exactly this commit's content, so a path-scoped\n438\t  `git commit <path>` in a dirty tree reviews only that content). The\n439\t  script never clears it; a relative value is made absolute against `pwd`.\n440\t  `ROAST_SKIP` (any non-empty value) bypasses entirely. `TMPDIR` (made\n441\t  absolute, else `/tmp`).\n442\t- **Steps**:\n443\t  1. `ROAST_SKIP` non-empty -> exit 0 silently.\n444\t  2. Local consent: `git config --local --get roast.gate`, lowercased and\n445\t     trimmed; not one of `enabled|enable|true|yes|on|1` -> exit 0 silently\n446\t     (a shared dispatcher's presence is not enrollment).\n447\t  3. Binary: `<git rev-parse --show-toplevel or .>/node_modules/.bin/roast`;\n448\t     not executable -> warn, exit 0. Never a `roast` on `PATH`.\n449\t  4. Temp dir `roast-gate.XXXXXX` under `TMPDIR`; failure -> warn, exit 0.\n450\t     Removed on exit.\n451\t  5. `\"$ROAST\" gate settings`; non-zero exit -> warn plus first 20 stderr\n452\t     lines, exit 0. Parse the first `timeout_seconds=` line (non-numeric or\n453\t     missing -> 180) and first `severity=` line (not one of the five\n454\t     uppercase levels -> `HIGH`).\n455\t  6. Warn that the review is starting, then run in the background:\n456\t     `\"$ROAST\" review --staged --quick --format both --max-severity <SEV>\n457\t     --task \"pre-commit gate\"`, stdout (JSON) and stderr (Markdown)\n458\t     captured to files.\n459\t  7. Watchdog when timeout > 0: poll once a second; at the deadline mark\n460\t     timed-out, send SIGTERM, wait up to 5 s, then SIGKILL.\n461\t  8. Timed out -> warn, exit 0.\n462\t  9. Empty stdout -> warn \"no result (exit rc)\" plus first 20 stderr\n463\t     lines, exit 0 (silence is never a pass).\n464\t  10. Exit 0 -> exit 0. Exit other than 0/1 -> warn plus first 40 stderr\n465\t      lines, exit 0.\n466\t  11. Exit 1 -> print the full captured stderr (the findings), warn that the\n467\t      commit is blocked and how to bypass, exit 1.\n468\t- **Output**: warnings go to stderr as `roast gate: <message>`.\n469\t- **CLI obligations** this places on the TS CLI: `gate settings` output\n470\t  format and defaults above; `review` accepts `--staged`, `--quick`,\n471\t  `--format both`, `--max-severity`, `--task`; review exit 1 means findings\n472\t  at or above `--max-severity` and nothing else; a review that produces a\n473\t  result writes non-empty JSON to stdout; bootstrap is suppressed when\n474\t  `GIT_INDEX_FILE` is set; SIGTERM ends the review promptly.\n475\t\n476\t### 2.13 `roast ignore`\n477\t\n478\t- No arguments. Git root of cwd; failure -> usage error whose message is\n479\t  the git-root error (`not inside a git repository`), exit 2.\n480\t- `ensureStateIgnored(repo) -> {path, added}` with `path =\n481\t  <repo>/.gitignore`:\n482\t  1. Read the file; ENOENT means empty; other errors -> `read <path>: ...`.\n483\t  2. Already ignored if any line, whitespace-trimmed, equals one of\n484\t     `/.roast/`, `/.roast`, `.roast/`, `.roast` -> `added = false`, no\n485\t     write.\n486\t  3. Otherwise append `/.roast/\\n`, prefixed with `\\n` when the file is\n487\t     non-empty and does not end in `\\n`. Open with append+create, mode\n488\t     `0o644` for a new file. Errors: `open <path>: ...`, `append <path>:\n489\t     ...`, `close <path>: ...`.\n490\t- stdout: added -> `added /.roast/ to <path>`; else `<path> already ignores\n491\t  /.roast/`. Running twice changes nothing the second time.\n492\t- `roast init` calls the same helper after writing the starter config and\n493\t  prints `added /.roast/ to <path>` only when it added the line.\n494\t\n495\t## 3. TypeScript module design\n496\t\n497\t`src/gate/`:\n498\t\n499\t- `pre-commit.sh` -- the Go file, byte-identical, imported with esbuild's\n500\t  `text` loader.\n501\t- `constants.ts` -- the 2.1 constants, `HOOK_SCRIPT`, `manualLine()`.\n502\t- `git-config.ts` -- `configGet(repo, key)`, `configSet`, `configUnset`,\n503\t  `resolveHookPath(repo, name)`, `hooksPathConfigured(repo)`. Uses the\n504\t  shared git `execFile` helper from `src/scope/` (or `src/git/`, whichever\n505\t  the scope area defines), with the caller's env passed through.\n506\t- `decision.ts`:\n507\t\n508\t  ```ts\n509\t  export type Decision = 'none'|'enabled'|'declined'\n510\t  export function readDecision(repo:string, env:Env):Promise<Decision>\n511\t  export function recordDecision(\n512\t      repo:string, d:Decision, env:Env\n513\t  ):Promise<void>\n514\t  export function recordNotice(repo:string, env:Env):Promise<void>\n515\t  ```\n516\t\n517\t- `hook.ts`:\n518\t\n519\t  ```ts\n520\t  export interface GateStatus {\n521\t      repo:string; decision:Decision; hookPath:string;\n522\t      sidecarPath:string; shared:boolean; exists:boolean;\n523\t      ours:boolean; appended:boolean; foreign:boolean;\n524\t      appendable:boolean; executable:boolean; stale:boolean;\n525\t      noticeSent:boolean;\n526\t  }\n527\t  export type InstallAction =\n528\t      'installed'|'appended'|'refreshed'|'up-to-date'|'manual'\n529\t  export type RemoveAction = 'removed'|'nothing'|'preserved'\n530\t  export function inspect(repo:string, env:Env):Promise<GateStatus>\n531\t  export function isActive(s:GateStatus):boolean\n532\t  export function summary(s:GateStatus):string\n533\t  export function install(repo:string, env:Env):\n534\t      Promise<{action:InstallAction, status:GateStatus}>\n535\t  export function remove(repo:string, env:Env):\n536\t      Promise<{action:RemoveAction, status:GateStatus}>\n537\t  export function appendable(body:Uint8Array):boolean\n538\t  ```\n539\t\n540\t  Internal: `appendedBlock`, `appendBlock`, `stripBlock`, `writeScript`,\n541\t  `writeSidecar`, `removeOwnedSidecar`, `refreshOwnedSidecar`,\n542\t  `sidecarCurrent`.\n543\t- `atomic.ts` -- `writeFileAtomic(path, body, mode)` (2.7), using\n544\t  `fs.promises.open(tmp, 'wx', 0o600)`, `crypto.randomBytes` for the name.\n545\t- `bootstrap.ts`:\n546\t\n547\t  ```ts\n548\t  export type Outcome = 'quiet'|'suppressed'|'satisfied'|'installed'|\n549\t      'refreshed'|'declined'|'hinted'\n550\t  export interface BootstrapOptions {\n551\t      repo:string;\n552\t      out:(line:string)=>void;\n553\t      env:Env;\n554\t      prompt?:(question:string)=>Promise<boolean>;\n555\t      noOffer:boolean;\n556\t  }\n557\t  export function bootstrap(o:BootstrapOptions):Promise<Outcome>\n558\t  ```\n559\t\n560\t`src/cli/`:\n561\t\n562\t- `gate.ts` -- the `gate` command group (yargs) with `enable`, `disable`,\n563\t  `status`, hidden `settings`; `GATE_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT = 180`,\n564\t  `GATE_DEFAULT_SEVERITY = 'HIGH'`.\n565\t- `config.ts` (shared with other areas) -- `gateConfigPath(repo)` and the\n566\t  `noGateConfig` usage error.\n567\t- `bootstrap-gate.ts` -- `maybeBootstrapGate(io)` called from the root and\n568\t  `review` handlers (yargs middleware or start of the handler, before\n569\t  anything else in the review), skipped for `--error-format json`. Uses\n570\t  `interactiveTerminals` and the shared line reader for the prompt.\n571\t- `ignore.ts` -- `ignore` command, `STATE_IGNORE_ENTRY`,\n572\t  `ensureStateIgnored(repo)` (exported for `init`).\n573\t\n574\tDependencies: `src/config` (`find`, `load`, gate section types),\n575\t`src/scope` (`gitRoot`, git exec helper), `src/record` (`STATE_DIR`),\n576\t`src/cli` prompt helpers (`interactiveTerminals`, `promptYesDefault`),\n577\tusage-error type and exit codes. Consumers: `src/cli/doctor.ts`\n578\t(`inspect`, `isActive`, `summary`), `src/cli/init.ts`\n579\t(`ensureStateIgnored`).\n580\t\n581\t## 4. Deliberate changes\n582\t\n583\tChange 19 (spec.md) applies here; the rest are resolved decisions and\n584\timplementation notes:\n585\t\n586\t- Windows is unsupported, so POSIX mode bits are always meaningful.\n587\t- Debug tracing under `roast:gate` may log actions and paths, never file\n588\t  bodies.\n589\t- U+2014 em dashes in Go's status and error strings are kept in the real\n590\t  output (written as `\\u2014` escapes in TS source); see 2.4 and spec.md\n591\t  \"Output strings\".\n592\t- A one-line hook file with no trailing newline gets a newline before\n593\t  Roast's block is appended (spec.md change 19; see 2.6 Append).\n594\t- The bootstrap prompt reads through the shared stdin reader, not a fresh\n595\t  buffered reader as in Go.\n596\t- A global or system `core.hooksPath` still affects `gate disable` (Go\n597\t  parity, kept; see 2.2 Shared).\n598\t- The Go bootstrap checks `term.IsTerminal` on the real stdin/stderr\n599\t  directly; the TS version uses the swappable `interactiveTerminals` seam\n600\t  (settled: terminal detection is swappable). Observable behavior on real\n601\t  terminals is unchanged.\n602\t\n603\t## 5. Test plan\n604\t\n605\tIsolation for every test that runs git: env `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null`,\n606\t`GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=/dev/null`, `GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1`; temp dirs resolved\n607\twith `realpath` (macOS `/var` -> `/private/var`); new repos set\n608\t`maintenance.auto=false`, `gc.auto=0`, `user.email`, `user.name`,\n609\t`commit.gpgsign=false` (the maintenance settings stop detached background\n610\t`git gc` racing temp-dir removal; Go pins this with\n611\t`TestRepoDisablesAutomaticMaintenance`). The in-process `run(argv, io)`\n612\tmust pass its injected env to git children. Assert on exit codes, file\n613\tcontents and modes, and local git config values, not on message text.\n614\t\n615\t**Hook installation and removal** -- CLI seam (`run(['gate','enable'])`,\n616\t`['gate','disable']`, `['gate','status']`) in a temp repo with a toplevel\n617\t`.roast.json`, then inspect files and `git config --local`:\n618\t\n619\t- Shipped script starts with the hook header (TestHookScriptCarriesMarker).\n620\t- Fresh repo inspects as not enrolled (TestInspectNotEnrolled).\n621\t- Enable writes HookScript with mode 0755 (TestInstallCreatesExecutableHook).\n622\t- A stale own hook is rewritten; a lost execute bit is repaired\n623\t  (TestInstallRefreshesStaleOwnHook, TestInstallRepairsLostExecuteBit).\n624\t- A foreign shell hook gains the block after its shebang plus a sidecar;\n625\t  a stale sidecar is refreshed (TestInstallAppendsToForeignShellHook,\n626\t  TestInstallRefreshesStaleSidecar).\n627\t- A non-shell hook is untouched and enable still records consent\n628\t  (TestInstallNeverTouchesNonShellHook, TestManualGateEnableRecordsConsent).\n629\t- A symlinked hook is foreign and its target untouched\n630\t  (TestInstallTreatsSymlinkedHookAsForeign).\n631\t- Disable deletes an own hook; strips only the block from a foreign hook\n632\t  (byte-identical remainder); leaves a foreign hook alone\n633\t  (TestRemoveDeletesOwnHook, TestRemoveStripsAppendedBlockOnly,\n634\t  TestRemoveLeavesForeignHookAlone).\n635\t- Ownership is anchored: marker text mid-file is not ours\n636\t  (TestOwnershipIsAnchored); a begin without an end is never stripped\n637\t  (TestMalformedAppendBlockIsNeverStripped); a marker pair without the\n638\t  invocation is foreign (TestMarkerPairWithoutInvocationIsForeign).\n639\t- Appending preserves the foreign hook's mode, including a missing execute\n640\t  bit (TestAppendPreservesForeignMode).\n641\t- A foreign file at the sidecar path is never overwritten or deleted\n642\t  (TestSidecarIsNeverClobbered, TestRemoveLeavesForeignSidecarAlone).\n643\t- A planted symlink at a predictable temp name is not followed\n644\t  (TestAtomicWriteDoesNotFollowAPlantedTempSymlink; keep the Go test's\n645\t  `pre-commit.roast-tmp` name and add one for `.pre-commit.roast-*`).\n646\t- `core.hooksPath` is honoured (TestHonorsCoreHooksPath).\n647\t- Decision round trip including aliases, and recording a decision clears\n648\t  the notice (TestDecisionRoundTrip, TestRecordDecisionClearsNotice).\n649\t- Appendability table from 2.5 (TestAppendable): drive through `gate\n650\t  enable` (appended vs untouched) or, if too slow, test `appendable`\n651\t  directly as a pure function.\n652\t- Enable refuses without a toplevel config (exit 2) and works with one\n653\t  (TestGateEnableRefusesConfigTheHookCannotSee,\n654\t  TestGateEnableWithToplevelConfig).\n655\t\n656\t**Shared dispatcher** (`core.hooksPath` pointing at a directory used by two\n657\trepos):\n658\t\n659\t- A shared hook does not review in a repo without local consent, even with\n660\t  a global `roast.gate=enabled` (TestSharedGateRequiresLocalConsent).\n661\t- Enrollment aliases agree between `readDecision` and the script\n662\t  (TestGateEnrollmentAliasesMatchDispatcher).\n663\t- Bootstrap does not adopt an inherited gate; refreshes a declined repo's\n664\t  stale legacy dispatcher (TestBootstrapDoesNotAdoptInheritedGate,\n665\t  TestBootstrapRefreshesDeclinedLegacyDispatcher).\n666\t- Disable preserves the dispatcher for the other repo, refreshes a legacy\n667\t  one, never touches a foreign sidecar\n668\t  (TestSharedGateDisablePreservesOtherRepository,\n669\t  TestSharedGateDisableRefreshesLegacyDispatchers,\n670\t  TestSharedGateDisableNeverTouchesForeignSidecar,\n671\t  TestGateCommandsKeepSharedDispatcher).\n672\t\n673\t**Bootstrap** -- CLI seam: `run(['review', ...])` against the fake\n674\tinference server (approved config), with `interactiveTerminals` simulated\n675\tand stdin answers supplied; assert `roast.gate`, `roast.gate-notice`, and\n676\thook presence:\n677\t\n678\t- A declined prompt is remembered and never re-asked\n679\t  (TestBootstrapPromptDeclineIsRemembered).\n680\t- Accepting installs and records `enabled`\n681\t  (TestBootstrapPromptAcceptsAndInstalls).\n682\t- Non-interactive runs hint once (`roast.gate-notice=sent`, no hook)\n683\t  (TestBootstrapNonInteractiveHintsOnce).\n684\t- `GIT_INDEX_FILE` set suppresses it (TestBootstrapSuppressesInsideHook).\n685\t- `gate.offer: false` never prompts or hints, and does not consume the\n686\t  notice (TestBootstrapNoOfferNeverPrompts,\n687\t  TestGateOfferFalseStopsTheGateOffer).\n688\t- `ROAST_NO_HOOK` has no effect (TestBootstrapIgnoresNoHookEnvironment,\n689\t  TestNoHookEnvironmentDoesNotStopTheGateOffer).\n690\t- No offer when the config is only in a subdirectory; offer with a\n691\t  toplevel config, also under `--format json`\n692\t  (TestReviewDoesNotOfferGateTheHookCannotRun,\n693\t  TestReviewOffersGateWithToplevelConfig). Observe via\n694\t  `roast.gate-notice`, not stderr text.\n695\t\n696\t**Gate settings** -- CLI seam:\n697\t\n698\t- Values come from the config, severity uppercased, env ignored\n699\t  (TestGateSettingsComeFromTheProjectConfig).\n700\t- Defaults 180 / HIGH (TestGateSettingsDefaultWhenUnset).\n701\t- No config -> exit 2 (TestGateSettingsWithoutProjectConfigIsAUsageError).\n702\t- Invalid `severity`, negative `timeout_seconds`, non-boolean `offer` ->\n703\t  exit 2 (TestInvalidGateSettingsAreRejected).\n704\t\n705\t**Hook execution** -- real `git commit` in a temp repo (spawned with\n706\t`execFile`), with a POSIX shell stub written at\n707\t`<repo>/node_modules/.bin/roast` (mode 0755). The stub answers `gate\n708\tsettings` from `STUB_TIMEOUT` / `STUB_SEVERITY` (optionally\n709\t`STUB_SETTINGS_EXIT`, `STUB_SETTINGS_STDERR`); for any other call it\n710\tappends `ARGS: $*`, the `git diff --cached --name-only HEAD` names, and the\n711\tfull `git diff --cached HEAD` to `$STUB_LOG`, then optionally sleeps\n712\t(`STUB_SLEEP`), prints `STUB_STDOUT` / `STUB_STDERR`, and exits\n713\t`STUB_EXIT`. An empty log means no review ran. The seeded repo has `a.txt`\n714\tstaged but not committed and `b.txt` committed by path (`git commit b.txt\n715\t-m ...`), with `roast.gate=enabled`. Port the stub verbatim. Assert commit\n716\tsuccess/failure and the log; where output must be checked, check for a\n717\ttest-controlled marker the stub printed, not the script's own wording.\n718\t\n719\t- Path-scoped commit reviews only `b.txt`'s content\n720\t  (TestGateReviewsOnlyThePathScopedCommitsContent).\n721\t- Exit 1 blocks and the stub's stderr reaches the user\n722\t  (TestGateBlocksOnFindingsAndPrintsThemToStderr).\n723\t- `ROAST_SKIP=1` skips without running the stub\n724\t  (TestGateSkipBypassesEntirely).\n725\t- Empty stdout allows (TestGateTreatsEmptyStdoutAsInfrastructureFailure).\n726\t- Other exits allow, including exit 2 for an untrusted config whose stderr\n727\t  reaches the user (TestGateAllowsCommitOnOperationalFailure,\n728\t  TestGateAllowsCommitWhenConfigIsUntrusted).\n729\t- Missing binary allows (TestGateAllowsCommitWhenRoastIsMissing).\n730\t- Timeout allows (TestGateTimesOutWithoutBlocking; sleeps, so gate behind\n731\t  an opt-out env for quick runs); timeout and severity come from `gate\n732\t  settings`, not env (TestGateTimeoutComesFromTheProjectRoast,\n733\t  TestGateSeverityComesFromTheProjectRoast); a failing `gate settings`\n734\t  allows (TestGateAllowsCommitWhenSettingsAreUnavailable).\n735\t- Appended block runs alongside a foreign hook, including one that exits\n736\t  early, and a non-executable hook does not run\n737\t  (TestGateRunsAlongsideAForeignHook,\n738\t  TestGateRunsInAForeignHookThatExitsEarly,\n739\t  TestGateDoesNotRunWhenHookIsNotExecutable).\n740\t\n741\tSince the script is unchanged, these tests mainly prove the TS install\n742\tpath writes a working hook; they need `sh` and `git` only, no Node build.\n743\t\n744\t**ignore** -- CLI seam (`run(['ignore'])`, `run(['init', ...])`):\n745\t\n746\t- Creates `.gitignore` containing `/.roast/\\n`\n747\t  (TestIgnoreCreatesToplevelGitignore).\n748\t- Appends, adding a newline to an unterminated last line\n749\t  (TestIgnoreAppendsToExistingGitignore).\n750\t- Leaves each equivalent entry form unchanged\n751\t  (TestIgnoreLeavesEquivalentEntryUnchanged).\n752\t- Second run is a no-op (TestIgnoreTwiceIsIdempotent).\n753\t- Outside a repository -> exit 2\n754\t  (TestIgnoreOutsideGitRepositoryIsUsageError).\n755\t- `init` adds the entry (TestInitIgnoresTheStateDirectory).\n756\t\n757\t## 6. Go baseline references\n758\t\n759\tAt commit `cd08f10`:\n760\t\n761\t- `internal/gate/gate.go`, `hook.go`, `bootstrap.go`, `pre-commit.sh`\n762\t- `internal/cli/gate.go`, `internal/cli/ignore.go`\n763\t- `internal/cli/cli.go` (`gateBootstrapCommands`, `PersistentPreRunE`,\n764\t  `maybeBootstrapGate`, exit codes)\n765\t- `internal/cli/config.go` (`gateConfigPath`, `errNoGateConfig`,\n766\t  `loadProjectConfig`)\n767\t- `internal/cli/prompt.go` (`promptYesDefault`)\n768\t- `internal/cli/doctor.go` (`doctorGitChecks`, consumer)\n769\t- `internal/cli/init.go` (consumer of `ensureStateIgnored`)\n770\t- `internal/config/config.go` (`Gate`, `Offers`, `validateSettings`,\n771\t  `Find`)\n772\t- Tests: `internal/gate/hook_test.go`, `hook_exec_test.go`,\n773\t  `bootstrap_test.go`, `shared_test.go`; `internal/cli/gate_test.go`,\n774\t  `gate_config_test.go`, `ignore_test.go`, `settings_test.go` (gate\n775\t  tests), `init_test.go` (`TestInitIgnoresTheStateDirectory`)\n776\t\n777\t## 7. Resolved\n778\t\n779\tResolved (maintainer decisions, see spec.md):\n780\t\n781\t1. Go's em dashes in status and error strings are kept as U+2014 in\n782\t   output, written as `\\u2014` escapes in TS source (spec.md cross-cutting\n783\t   \"Output strings\"); `pre-commit.sh` bytes are unchanged.\n784\t2. A global `core.hooksPath` affecting `gate disable` stays as Go parity\n785\t   (spec.md Further Notes).\n786\t3. A one-line hook with no trailing newline gets a newline before Roast's\n787\t   block is appended (spec.md change 19).\n788\t4. The bootstrap prompt uses the one shared stdin reader.\n789\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"776ac9e1-0ccd-4600-8cd0-2b17f1742875","uuid":"8c04c05c-fde8-4b3c-85ea-3ea39a18a9a1","timestamp":"2026-11-18T20:09:53.084Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/.claude/projects/-Users-nick-code-roast-ts-rewrite-29-gate-commands-and-ignore/776ac9e1-0ccd-4600-8cd0-2b17f1742875/tool-results/bezo6rx3q.txt","content":"# Area 12: Gate and `ignore`\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nThe **gate** is the pre-commit hook that runs a quick review of exactly the\nstaged content of a commit and fails open: only a finding at or above the\nconfigured severity blocks the commit; every operational failure prints a\nwarning and lets the commit through.\n\nThis area owns:\n\n- the hook script (`pre-commit.sh`, shipped unchanged from Go) and its\n  contract with the CLI;\n- installing, refreshing, inspecting, and removing the hook in a repository\n  (`roast gate enable|disable|status`), including coexistence with a\n  **foreign** (someone else's) pre-commit hook and with a shared\n  `core.hooksPath` dispatcher;\n- the per-repository enrollment decision stored in local Git config;\n- the hidden `roast gate settings` query the hook makes;\n- the **review-time bootstrap**: the one-time offer, made before a review\n  runs, to enable the gate;\n- `roast ignore` (and the helper `init` reuses), which adds `/.roast/` to\n  the toplevel `.gitignore` so run records are not committed.\n\nThe gate reads only a project config at the Git toplevel, because the hook\nruns from the toplevel without `--config`.\n\n## 2. Behavior contract\n\n### 2.1 Constants\n\n| Name | Value |\n|------|-------|\n| hook name | `pre-commit` |\n| sidecar name | `roast-pre-commit` |\n| hook marker | `# roast-gate-hook: v1` |\n| hook header | `\"#!/bin/sh\\n# roast-gate-hook: v1\\n\"` |\n| append begin marker | see 2.6 |\n| append end marker | `# <<< roast pre-commit gate <<<` |\n| decision config key | `roast.gate` |\n| notice config key | `roast.gate-notice` (value written: `sent`) |\n| default gate timeout | `180` seconds |\n| default gate severity | `HIGH` |\n| state ignore entry | `/.roast/` (from the run-record state dir `.roast`) |\n\n**Manual line** -- the one line that invokes the sidecar; it is both the\nbody of the appended block and what a user adds by hand to a hook Roast\nwill not edit:\n\n```sh\n\"$(git rev-parse --git-path hooks/roast-pre-commit)\" || exit $?\n```\n\n**HookScript** is the byte-exact content of `pre-commit.sh` (it starts with\nthe hook header). Every \"is it current\" check is an exact byte comparison\nagainst it. Because the TS version ships the identical file, hooks\ninstalled by the Go version compare equal and are not reported stale. The\nfile must reach `dist/cli.js` byte-for-byte (esbuild `text` loader; no\nreformatting, LF line endings).\n\n### 2.2 Git plumbing\n\nAll Git calls are `git -C <repo> ...` where `<repo>` is the working-tree\nroot from `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` (the scope area's `gitRoot`).\n\n- **Hook path resolution** (`resolveHookPath(repo, name)`):\n  `git -C <repo> rev-parse --git-path hooks/<name>`, stdout trimmed. Non-zero\n  exit -> error `resolve hooks path in <repo>: <err>`; empty output -> error\n  `resolve hooks path in <repo>: git returned nothing`. A relative result is\n  joined onto `<repo>`. Git itself honours `core.hooksPath` and, in a linked\n  worktree, the common git dir (hooks are shared across worktrees). Used for\n  both `hooks/pre-commit` (the hook path) and `hooks/roast-pre-commit` (the\n  sidecar path).\n- **Shared** = `git -C <repo> config --get core.hooksPath` exits 0. Note:\n  no `--local`; a global or system `core.hooksPath` also counts.\n- **Config get** (`--local`): `git -C <repo> config --local --get <key>`;\n  any failure reads as `\"\"`; output trimmed.\n- **Config set**: `git -C <repo> config --local <key> <value>`; failure ->\n  error `git config <key>: <err>: <trimmed combined output>`.\n- **Config unset**: `git -C <repo> config --local --unset <key>`; callers\n  ignore its failure (exit 5 means \"not set\").\n\n### 2.3 Enrollment decision\n\n`Decision` is one of `none` (Go `\"\"`), `enabled`, `declined`.\n\n`readDecision`: local `roast.gate`, trimmed and lowercased:\n\n- `enabled | enable | true | yes | on | 1` -> `enabled`\n- `declined | disabled | false | no | off | 0` -> `declined`\n- anything else, including unset -> `none` (a typo means \"unanswered\")\n\nThe hook script accepts exactly the same enabled aliases (it reads with\n`--local`, so a global `roast.gate` never enrolls a repo).\n\n`recordDecision(repo, d)`: first unset `roast.gate-notice` (ignore errors);\nthen if `d` is `none` unset `roast.gate` (ignore errors) and return;\notherwise set `roast.gate` to `enabled` or `declined`.\n\n`recordNotice(repo)`: set `roast.gate-notice` to `sent`.\n\n### 2.4 Inspect (never mutates)\n\n`inspect(repo) -> Status` with fields `repo`, `decision`, `hookPath`,\n`sidecarPath`, `shared`, `exists`, `ours`, `appended`, `foreign`,\n`appendable`, `executable`, `stale`, `noticeSent`. At most one of `ours`,\n`appended`, `foreign` is true.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Resolve hook path and sidecar path (errors propagate). Set `shared`,\n   `decision`, `noticeSent` (= local `roast.gate-notice` non-empty).\n2. `lstat(hookPath)`. ENOENT -> return (all file flags false). Other error\n   -> `stat <path>: <err>`.\n3. `exists = true`; `executable = (lstat mode & 0o100) != 0` (owner execute\n   bit; Git silently skips a hook without it).\n4. A symlink is `foreign` (never appendable); return.\n5. Read the file (error -> `read <path>: <err>`). Classify:\n   - body starts with the hook header -> `ours`;\n     `stale = body !== HookScript || !executable`.\n   - else if the body contains a valid appended block (2.6) -> `appended`;\n     `stale = !sidecarCurrent(sidecarPath)`. The foreign file's own mode\n     never feeds `stale` (Roast does not repair it); it feeds `active`.\n   - else `foreign`; `appendable = appendable(bodyBytes)`.\n\n`sidecarCurrent(path)`: `stat` (follows symlinks) succeeds, owner execute\nbit set, and content equals HookScript.\n\n`active(status) = decision === enabled && (ours || appended) && executable`.\n\n**Summary** (one line, first match wins; `<p>` is `hookPath`). The Go\nstrings use an em dash (U+2014), and so does the real TS output: the\ncharacter is kept and written as the escape `\\u2014` in TS source (spec.md\ncross-cutting \"Output strings\"). Where this spec writes `--` inside these\nquoted output strings, read it as U+2014; `pre-commit.sh` bytes are\nunchanged:\n\n1. `(ours||appended) && !executable`: `INSTALLED BUT NOT RUNNING -- <p> is\n   not executable, so git skips it (chmod +x it, or ``roast gate enable``\n   for roast's own hook)`\n2. `(ours||appended) && stale`: ``installed dispatcher is stale -- run\n   `roast gate enable` to refresh: <p>``\n3. `(ours||appended) && decision=declined`: `declined for this repo;\n   dispatcher retained: <p>`\n4. `(ours||appended) && decision!=enabled`: ``dispatcher installed but not\n   enrolled in this repo (`roast gate enable` enables it): <p>``\n5. `ours`: `installed: <p>`\n6. `appended`: `installed via an appended block in a foreign hook: <p>`\n7. `foreign && declined`: `declined; a foreign pre-commit hook is present\n   (untouched): <p>`\n8. `foreign && appendable`: ``not installed -- a foreign pre-commit hook is\n   present (untouched); `roast gate enable` appends to it: <p>``\n9. `foreign`: `not installed -- a foreign pre-commit hook is present and is\n   not an appendable shell script (untouched): <p>`\n10. `declined`: ``declined for this repo (`roast gate enable` turns it on)``\n11. `enabled`: ``enabled for this repo but the hook is missing -- run\n    `roast gate enable` to reinstall``\n12. otherwise: ``not enrolled (`roast gate enable` installs it)``\n\nThe doctor area's `git-gate` check consumes `inspect`, `stale`, `active`,\nand `summary` (warn when `stale || (enabled && !active)`).\n\n### 2.5 Appendable foreign hooks\n\n`appendable(bytes)` is deliberately conservative:\n\n1. Empty, or not valid UTF-8 -> false. (Check validity on the raw bytes,\n   e.g. `new TextDecoder('utf-8', {fatal:true})`; do not decode lossily\n   first.)\n2. First line (up to the first `\\n`), strip one trailing `\\r`, trim\n   whitespace. Must start with `#!`, else false.\n3. Split the rest on whitespace; none -> false. `interp = basename(f[0])`.\n4. If `interp === 'env'`: need `f[1]`, else false; `f[1]` starting with\n   `-` or containing `=` -> false; `interp = basename(f[1])`.\n5. True iff `interp` is one of `sh`, `bash`, `dash`, `ksh`, `zsh`.\n\nPinned cases: `#!/bin/sh\\n`, `#!/bin/bash -e\\n`, `#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n`,\n`#!/usr/bin/env zsh\\nx\\n` -> true; `#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n`,\n`#!/usr/bin/perl\\n`, `#!/usr/bin/env -S bash\\n`, `no shebang\\n`, `\"\"`,\n`\"\\x00\\x01binary\"` -> false.\n\n### 2.6 The appended block\n\nMarkers, each a whole line:\n\n```text\n# >>> roast pre-commit gate (managed by `roast gate`) >>>\n# <<< roast pre-commit gate <<<\n```\n\nBlock text inserted (note the leading blank line):\n\n```text\n\n# >>> roast pre-commit gate (managed by `roast gate`) >>>\n# Added by `roast gate enable`. Delete this block (or run\n# `roast gate disable`) to remove the gate; the rest of this file is yours.\n\"$(git rev-parse --git-path hooks/roast-pre-commit)\" || exit $?\n# <<< roast pre-commit gate <<<\n```\n\ni.e. `\"\\n\" + begin + \"\\n\" + comment1 + \"\\n\" + comment2 + \"\\n\" +\nmanualLine + \"\\n\" + end + \"\\n\"`.\n\n**Detection** (`appendedBlock(lines)`, lines = body split on `\\n`): scan\nlines, comparing each trimmed line. A line equal to the begin marker sets\n`start = i` and clears `hasInvocation`. A line equal to the end marker while\n`start >= 0`: if `hasInvocation`, return `[start, i]`; otherwise reset\n`start = -1`. A line equal to the manual line while `start >= 0` sets\n`hasInvocation`. No match -> not found. So: markers alone are not\nauthorship; a begin without an end is not a block; edits to the comment\nlines inside a block keep it recognizable. Ownership is anchored: `ours`\nrequires the header at byte 0, never \"contains the marker somewhere\".\n\n**Append** (`appendBlock(path)`): read bytes; mode = current permission\nbits (fallback `0o755` if stat fails) -- preserved exactly, execute bit\nincluded, so a hook the owner `chmod -x`'d stays disabled. Find the first\n`\\n`; none -> the file is a one-line hook with no trailing newline\n(`appendable` accepts it): append a `\\n` to the body first, then proceed\n(deliberate change 19; Go failed here with `append gate to <path>: no\ncomplete shebang line` and `gate enable` exited 4). Write\n`body[..=nl] + block + body[nl+1..]` atomically with that mode. The\nblock goes right after the shebang (not at EOF) because a hook ending in\n`exit 0` or `exec ...` would never reach a tail block. Consequence: Roast\nruns first, and a blocking review stops the foreign hook from running.\n\n**Strip** (`stripBlock(path)`): read; keep mode (fallback `0o755`); split on\n`\\n`; no valid block -> error `remove gate from <path>: the roast block has\nno closing marker; left the file untouched (delete the block by hand)`. If\nthe line before `start` is blank (trimmed empty), include it in the removed\nrange. Rejoin the remaining lines with `\\n` and write atomically. Every\nother byte is preserved.\n\n### 2.7 Writing files\n\n- **writeFileAtomic(path, body, mode)**: create a temp file in\n  `dirname(path)` named `.<basename>.roast-<random>` with exclusive create\n  (`O_CREAT|O_EXCL`, mode `0o600`, unpredictable name; retry on `EEXIST`),\n  write, `fchmod(mode)`, close, `rename` over `path`; remove the temp file on\n  any failure. Never use a predictable temp name: `core.hooksPath` can point\n  inside the working tree (`.githooks`), where a checked-out symlink at a\n  predictable temp path would redirect the write. Errors: `create temp file\n  for <path>: ...`, `write <tmp>: ...`, `chmod <tmp>: ...`, `close <tmp>:\n  ...`, `replace <path>: ...`.\n- **writeScript(path, body)**: `mkdir -p dirname(path)` (mode `0o755`;\n  error `mkdir <dir>: ...`), then `writeFileAtomic(path, body, 0o755)`.\n- **writeSidecar(path)**: `lstat`; symlink -> error ``<path> is a symlink\n  roast did not create; move it aside and re-run `roast gate enable` ``;\n  exists and content does not start with the hook header -> error\n  ``<path> already exists and was not written by roast; move it aside and\n  re-run `roast gate enable` ``; other stat error -> `stat <path>: ...`.\n  Otherwise `writeScript(path, HookScript)`.\n- **removeOwnedSidecar(path)**: absent -> ok; symlink -> leave; content not\n  starting with the header -> leave; else delete (ENOENT ignored).\n- **refreshOwnedSidecar(path)**: absent -> ok; not a regular file -> leave;\n  starts with header and differs from HookScript -> `writeSidecar(path)`;\n  else nothing. Never creates a sidecar.\n\n### 2.8 Install\n\n`install(repo) -> {action, status}` never records a decision (callers do).\nUses `status = inspect(repo)` (the pre-install status is returned):\n\n| State | Effect | Action |\n|-------|--------|--------|\n| foreign, not appendable | `writeSidecar` only; hook untouched | `manual` |\n| foreign, appendable | `writeSidecar`; `appendBlock(hookPath)` | `appended` |\n| appended, not stale | none | `up-to-date` |\n| appended, stale | `writeSidecar` | `refreshed` |\n| ours, not stale | none | `up-to-date` |\n| ours, stale | `writeScript(hookPath, HookScript)`, fixes mode | `refreshed` |\n| no hook | `writeScript(hookPath, HookScript)` | `installed` |\n\n### 2.9 Remove\n\n`remove(repo) -> {action, status}`:\n\n1. `status = inspect(repo)`.\n2. If `shared`: when `(ours || appended) && stale`, run `install(repo)`\n   (older dispatchers lack the consent check); then\n   `refreshOwnedSidecar(sidecarPath)`; return `preserved`. The shared\n   dispatcher is never deleted.\n3. Otherwise: `ours` -> delete hook (ENOENT ignored; error `remove <path>:\n   ...`), action `removed`; `appended` -> `stripBlock`, action `removed`;\n   else `nothing`.\n4. In every non-shared case, `removeOwnedSidecar(sidecarPath)` (an error\n   here returns the action computed so far plus the error).\n\n### 2.10 Commands\n\nAll gate subcommands take no positional arguments (extra args -> usage\nerror, exit 2). `roast gate` with no subcommand prints help, exit 0.\nErrors that are not usage errors exit 4 (the CLI's generic code).\n\n**`roast gate enable`**\n\n1. Git root of cwd; failure -> usage error `not inside a Git repository`.\n2. `gateConfigPath(repo)` = project-config search starting and stopping at\n   the toplevel (only `<toplevel>/.roast.json`, a non-directory). Search\n   error -> usage error with that message. Not found -> usage error:\n   ``the pre-commit gate runs from the Git toplevel and finds no\n   .roast.json there; put the project config at the toplevel (`npx roast\n   init`) before enabling the gate``. The config is not loaded,\n   validated, or trust-checked.\n3. `install(repo)`, then `recordDecision(repo, enabled)` -- also for\n   `manual`.\n4. Output on stdout:\n   - `manual`: ``<hookPath> is not an appendable shell script; Roast left\n     it untouched.\\nAdd this line manually:\\n\\n    <manualLine>\\n`` and\n     stop.\n   - `installed`: `gate installed: <hookPath>`\n   - `appended`: `gate appended to existing hook: <hookPath>`\n   - `refreshed`: `gate refreshed: <hookPath>`\n   - `up-to-date`: `gate already up to date: <hookPath>`\n   - then, for all of the above four: `bypass one commit with: ROAST_SKIP=1\n     git commit ...`\n\n**`roast gate disable`** (no config required)\n\n1. Git root; failure -> usage error `not inside a Git repository`.\n2. `remove(repo)`, then `recordDecision(repo, declined)`.\n3. stdout: `removed` -> `gate removed from <hookPath>`; `preserved` ->\n   `gate disabled for this repository; shared dispatcher preserved at\n   <hookPath>`; otherwise `no Roast gate was installed; recorded the\n   decline`.\n\n**`roast gate status`**\n\n1. Git root; failure -> usage error `not inside a Git repository`.\n2. `inspect(repo)`; print exactly three lines (labels padded to align):\n\n   ```text\n   repo:     <repo>\n   gate:     <summary>\n   decision: <enabled|declined|none recorded>\n   ```\n\n**`roast gate settings`** (hidden from help)\n\n- Flag `--config <path>` (default: nearest `.roast.json` from cwd up to\n  the toplevel, the standard project-config lookup). Loads the config the\n  standard way (all failures are usage errors, exit 2; a missing config\n  names `npx roast init`). No trust check.\n- stdout, exactly: `timeout_seconds=<n>\\nseverity=<SEV>\\n` where `n` is\n  `gate.timeout_seconds` or 180, and `SEV` is `gate.severity` uppercased or\n  `HIGH`. Environment variables never affect these values (the retired\n  `ROAST_GATE_TIMEOUT` / `ROAST_GATE_SEVERITY` are ignored).\n\nConfig validation of the `gate` section belongs to the config area and is\nrestated here for completeness: `timeout_seconds` integer >= 0 (0 disables\nthe watchdog); `severity` case-insensitively one of `INFO`, `LOW`,\n`MEDIUM`, `HIGH`, `CRITICAL`; `offer` boolean, unset means true. Invalid\nvalues fail any config load with a usage error (exit 2).\n\n### 2.11 Review-time bootstrap\n\nRuns before the review itself (before trust, scope, or any network) when\nthe invoked command is the bare root command or `review`, and\n`--error-format` is not `json` (`--format json` does not suppress it).\nNothing here can fail the review: all failures are silent or printed as a\nwarning.\n\n**Preconditions** (any failing -> do nothing, silently):\n\n1. cwd is in a Git repository (`repo` = toplevel).\n2. `gateConfigPath(repo)` finds `<toplevel>/.roast.json` without error.\n   A config only in a subdirectory never triggers an offer, since the hook\n   could not see it.\n3. That file loads (raw config load; no trust check, no stored\n   credentials). A load error is silent here; the review reports it.\n\n**Options**: `noOffer = gate.offer === false`; a `prompt` function exists\nonly when stdin and stderr are both terminals (use the swappable\n`interactiveTerminals` seam). The prompt writes `<question> [Y/n] ` to\nstderr and reads one line from the one shared stdin reader (the same\nreader the rest of the CLI uses, never a fresh buffered reader): `\"\"`,\n`y`, `yes` (case-insensitive,\ntrimmed) -> yes; EOF with no input -> no; anything else -> no. Messages go\nto stderr as `roast: <message>\\n`. If bootstrap returns an error, print\n`roast: pre-commit gate setup skipped: <err>` to stderr and continue.\n\n**Algorithm** (`bootstrap`, returns an outcome: `quiet`, `suppressed`,\n`satisfied`, `installed`, `refreshed`, `declined`, `hinted`):\n\n1. If `noOffer`, or env `GIT_INDEX_FILE` is non-empty (we are inside a Git\n   hook, e.g. the gate's own review), or `repo` is empty -> `suppressed`.\n   `ROAST_NO_HOOK` has no effect.\n2. `status = inspect(repo)`.\n3. If `shared`: `refreshOwnedSidecar(sidecarPath)`.\n4. If `decision !== enabled && (ours || appended) && stale`: `install(repo)`\n   (refreshes only a recognized Roast dispatcher, never a foreign hook, so\n   an inherited old shared dispatcher gains the consent check), then\n   re-`inspect`.\n5. `declined` -> `quiet`.\n6. `enabled` -> `satisfied` if `active && !stale`; otherwise run the\n   install step below without recording.\n7. (decision `none`) If `foreign && !appendable` -> hint: ``this repo's\n   pre-commit hook is not an appendable shell script, so Roast left it\n   untouched; run `roast gate enable` to install the sidecar and print the\n   line to add``.\n8. No `prompt` -> hint: ``no pre-commit gate in this repo; run `roast gate\n   enable` to install it (non-interactive runs never install Git hooks\n   without consent)``.\n9. Ask: `Install the Roast pre-commit gate in this repository (<repo>)?`,\n   or when `foreign`: `This repository already has a pre-commit hook.\n   Append the Roast gate to it (<hookPath>)?`. Prompt error -> return it.\n10. No -> `recordDecision(declined)`; print ``gate declined for this\n    repository; `roast gate enable` turns it on later``; `declined`.\n11. Yes -> install step with recording.\n\n**Install step** (`record` flag): `install(repo)`.\n\n- `manual`: if `record`, `recordDecision(enabled)`; then hint: ``this\n  repo's pre-commit hook cannot be appended to, so Roast left it untouched;\n  add this line to enable the gate:\\n    <manualLine>``.\n- otherwise, if `record`, `recordDecision(enabled)`; then `installed` ->\n  print `pre-commit gate installed: <hookPath> (bypass one commit with\n  ROAST_SKIP=1)`, outcome `installed`; `appended` -> print `pre-commit gate\n  appended to the existing hook: <hookPath>`, outcome `installed`;\n  `refreshed` -> outcome `refreshed` (silent); else `satisfied`.\n\n**Hint** (this is \"the gate hint printed during review\"): if\n`noticeSent`, return `quiet` without printing. Otherwise print the message,\n`recordNotice(repo)`, return `hinted` (a `recordNotice` failure is returned\nas the error). A hint is printed at most once per repository until a\ndecision is recorded (recording a decision clears the notice). A\nsuppressed offer (`gate.offer: false`) does not consume the notice.\n\nThe CLI messages here say bare `roast` (not `npx roast`); that is a code\nstring, kept as is.\n\n### 2.12 Hook script contract (`pre-commit.sh`, shipped unchanged)\n\nInstalled as the hook (mode `0o755`) or as the sidecar. Interface:\n\n- **Inputs**: Git's hook environment, above all `GIT_INDEX_FILE` (the\n  temporary index holding exactly this commit's content, so a path-scoped\n  `git commit <path>` in a dirty tree reviews only that content). The\n  script never clears it; a relative value is made absolute against `pwd`.\n  `ROAST_SKIP` (any non-empty value) bypasses entirely. `TMPDIR` (made\n  absolute, else `/tmp`).\n- **Steps**:\n  1. `ROAST_SKIP` non-empty -> exit 0 silently.\n  2. Local consent: `git config --local --get roast.gate`, lowercased and\n     trimmed; not one of `enabled|enable|true|yes|on|1` -> exit 0 silently\n     (a shared dispatcher's presence is not enrollment).\n  3. Binary: `<git rev-parse --show-toplevel or .>/node_modules/.bin/roast`;\n     not executable -> warn, exit 0. Never a `roast` on `PATH`.\n  4. Temp dir `roast-gate.XXXXXX` under `TMPDIR`; failure -> warn, exit 0.\n     Removed on exit.\n  5. `\"$ROAST\" gate settings`; non-zero exit -> warn plus first 20 stderr\n     lines, exit 0. Parse the first `timeout_seconds=` line (non-numeric or\n     missing -> 180) and first `severity=` line (not one of the five\n     uppercase levels -> `HIGH`).\n  6. Warn that the review is starting, then run in the background:\n     `\"$ROAST\" review --staged --quick --format both --max-severity <SEV>\n     --task \"pre-commit gate\"`, stdout (JSON) and stderr (Markdown)\n     captured to files.\n  7. Watchdog when timeout > 0: poll once a second; at the deadline mark\n     timed-out, send SIGTERM, wait up to 5 s, then SIGKILL.\n  8. Timed out -> warn, exit 0.\n  9. Empty stdout -> warn \"no result (exit rc)\" plus first 20 stderr\n     lines, exit 0 (silence is never a pass).\n  10. Exit 0 -> exit 0. Exit other than 0/1 -> warn plus first 40 stderr\n      lines, exit 0.\n  11. Exit 1 -> print the full captured stderr (the findings), warn that the\n      commit is blocked and how to bypass, exit 1.\n- **Output**: warnings go to stderr as `roast gate: <message>`.\n- **CLI obligations** this places on the TS CLI: `gate settings` output\n  format and defaults above; `review` accepts `--staged`, `--quick`,\n  `--format both`, `--max-severity`, `--task`; review exit 1 means findings\n  at or above `--max-severity` and nothing else; a review that produces a\n  result writes non-empty JSON to stdout; bootstrap is suppressed when\n  `GIT_INDEX_FILE` is set; SIGTERM ends the review promptly.\n\n### 2.13 `roast ignore`\n\n- No arguments. Git root of cwd; failure -> usage error whose message is\n  the git-root error (`not inside a git repository`), exit 2.\n- `ensureStateIgnored(repo) -> {path, added}` with `path =\n  <repo>/.gitignore`:\n  1. Read the file; ENOENT means empty; other errors -> `read <path>: ...`.\n  2. Already ignored if any line, whitespace-trimmed, equals one of\n     `/.roast/`, `/.roast`, `.roast/`, `.roast` -> `added = false`, no\n     write.\n  3. Otherwise append `/.roast/\\n`, prefixed with `\\n` when the file is\n     non-empty and does not end in `\\n`. Open with append+create, mode\n     `0o644` for a new file. Errors: `open <path>: ...`, `append <path>:\n     ...`, `close <path>: ...`.\n- stdout: added -> `added /.roast/ to <path>`; else `<path> already ignores\n  /.roast/`. Running twice changes nothing the second time.\n- `roast init` calls the same helper after writing the starter config and\n  prints `added /.roast/ to <path>` only when it added the line.\n\n## 3. TypeScript module design\n\n`src/gate/`:\n\n- `pre-commit.sh` -- the Go file, byte-identical, imported with esbuild's\n  `text` loader.\n- `constants.ts` -- the 2.1 constants, `HOOK_SCRIPT`, `manualLine()`.\n- `git-config.ts` -- `configGet(repo, key)`, `configSet`, `configUnset`,\n  `resolveHookPath(repo, name)`, `hooksPathConfigured(repo)`. Uses the\n  shared git `execFile` helper from `src/scope/` (or `src/git/`, whichever\n  the scope area defines), with the caller's env passed through.\n- `decision.ts`:\n\n  ```ts\n  export type Decision = 'none'|'enabled'|'declined'\n  export function readDecision(repo:string, env:Env):Promise<Decision>\n  export function recordDecision(\n      repo:string, d:Decision, env:Env\n  ):Promise<void>\n  export function recordNotice(repo:string, env:Env):Promise<void>\n  ```\n\n- `hook.ts`:\n\n  ```ts\n  export interface GateStatus {\n      repo:string; decision:Decision; hookPath:string;\n      sidecarPath:string; shared:boolean; exists:boolean;\n      ours:boolean; appended:boolean; foreign:boolean;\n      appendable:boolean; executable:boolean; stale:boolean;\n      noticeSent:boolean;\n  }\n  export type InstallAction =\n      'installed'|'appended'|'refreshed'|'up-to-date'|'manual'\n  export type RemoveAction = 'removed'|'nothing'|'preserved'\n  export function inspect(repo:string, env:Env):Promise<GateStatus>\n  export function isActive(s:GateStatus):boolean\n  export function summary(s:GateStatus):string\n  export function install(repo:string, env:Env):\n      Promise<{action:InstallAction, status:GateStatus}>\n  export function remove(repo:string, env:Env):\n      Promise<{action:RemoveAction, status:GateStatus}>\n  export function appendable(body:Uint8Array):boolean\n  ```\n\n  Internal: `appendedBlock`, `appendBlock`, `stripBlock`, `writeScript`,\n  `writeSidecar`, `removeOwnedSidecar`, `refreshOwnedSidecar`,\n  `sidecarCurrent`.\n- `atomic.ts` -- `writeFileAtomic(path, body, mode)` (2.7), using\n  `fs.promises.open(tmp, 'wx', 0o600)`, `crypto.randomBytes` for the name.\n- `bootstrap.ts`:\n\n  ```ts\n  export type Outcome = 'quiet'|'suppressed'|'satisfied'|'installed'|\n      'refreshed'|'declined'|'hinted'\n  export interface BootstrapOptions {\n      repo:string;\n      out:(line:string)=>void;\n      env:Env;\n      prompt?:(question:string)=>Promise<boolean>;\n      noOffer:boolean;\n  }\n  export function bootstrap(o:BootstrapOptions):Promise<Outcome>\n  ```\n\n`src/cli/`:\n\n- `gate.ts` -- the `gate` command group (yargs) with `enable`, `disable`,\n  `status`, hidden `settings`; `GATE_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT = 180`,\n  `GATE_DEFAULT_SEVERITY = 'HIGH'`.\n- `config.ts` (shared with other areas) -- `gateConfigPath(repo)` and the\n  `noGateConfig` usage error.\n- `bootstrap-gate.ts` -- `maybeBootstrapGate(io)` called from the root and\n  `review` handlers (yargs middleware or start of the handler, before\n  anything else in the review), skipped for `--error-format json`. Uses\n  `interactiveTerminals` and the shared line reader for the prompt.\n- `ignore.ts` -- `ignore` command, `STATE_IGNORE_ENTRY`,\n  `ensureStateIgnored(repo)` (exported for `init`).\n\nDependencies: `src/config` (`find`, `load`, gate section types),\n`src/scope` (`gitRoot`, git exec helper), `src/record` (`STATE_DIR`),\n`src/cli` prompt helpers (`interactiveTerminals`, `promptYesDefault`),\nusage-error type and exit codes. Consumers: `src/cli/doctor.ts`\n(`inspect`, `isActive`, `summary`), `src/cli/init.ts`\n(`ensureStateIgnored`).\n\n## 4. Deliberate changes\n\nChange 19 (spec.md) applies here; the rest are resolved decisions and\nimplementation notes:\n\n- Windows is unsupported, so POSIX mode bits are always meaningful.\n- Debug tracing under `roast:gate` may log actions and paths, never file\n  bodies.\n- U+2014 em dashes in Go's status and error strings are kept in the real\n  output (written as `\\u2014` escapes in TS source); see 2.4 and spec.md\n  \"Output strings\".\n- A one-line hook file with no trailing newline gets a newline before\n  Roast's block is appended (spec.md change 19; see 2.6 Append).\n- The bootstrap prompt reads through the shared stdin reader, not a fresh\n  buffered reader as in Go.\n- A global or system `core.hooksPath` still affects `gate disable` (Go\n  parity, kept; see 2.2 Shared).\n- The Go bootstrap checks `term.IsTerminal` on the real stdin/stderr\n  directly; the TS version uses the swappable `interactiveTerminals` seam\n  (settled: terminal detection is swappable). Observable behavior on real\n  terminals is unchanged.\n\n## 5. Test plan\n\nIsolation for every test that runs git: env `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null`,\n`GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=/dev/null`, `GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1`; temp dirs resolved\nwith `realpath` (macOS `/var` -> `/private/var`); new repos set\n`maintenance.auto=false`, `gc.auto=0`, `user.email`, `user.name`,\n`commit.gpgsign=false` (the maintenance settings stop detached background\n`git gc` racing temp-dir removal; Go pins this with\n`TestRepoDisablesAutomaticMaintenance`). The in-process `run(argv, io)`\nmust pass its injected env to git children. Assert on exit codes, file\ncontents and modes, and local git config values, not on message text.\n\n**Hook installation and removal** -- CLI seam (`run(['gate','enable'])`,\n`['gate','disable']`, `['gate','status']`) in a temp repo with a toplevel\n`.roast.json`, then inspect files and `git config --local`:\n\n- Shipped script starts with the hook header (TestHookScriptCarriesMarker).\n- Fresh repo inspects as not enrolled (TestInspectNotEnrolled).\n- Enable writes HookScript with mode 0755 (TestInstallCreatesExecutableHook).\n- A stale own hook is rewritten; a lost execute bit is repaired\n  (TestInstallRefreshesStaleOwnHook, TestInstallRepairsLostExecuteBit).\n- A foreign shell hook gains the block after its shebang plus a sidecar;\n  a stale sidecar is refreshed (TestInstallAppendsToForeignShellHook,\n  TestInstallRefreshesStaleSidecar).\n- A non-shell hook is untouched and enable still records consent\n  (TestInstallNeverTouchesNonShellHook, TestManualGateEnableRecordsConsent).\n- A symlinked hook is foreign and its target untouched\n  (TestInstallTreatsSymlinkedHookAsForeign).\n- Disable deletes an own hook; strips only the block from a foreign hook\n  (byte-identical remainder); leaves a foreign hook alone\n  (TestRemoveDeletesOwnHook, TestRemoveStripsAppendedBlockOnly,\n  TestRemoveLeavesForeignHookAlone).\n- Ownership is anchored: marker text mid-file is not ours\n  (TestOwnershipIsAnchored); a begin without an end is never stripped\n  (TestMalformedAppendBlockIsNeverStripped); a marker pair without the\n  invocation is foreign (TestMarkerPairWithoutInvocationIsForeign).\n- Appending preserves the foreign hook's mode, including a missing execute\n  bit (TestAppendPreservesForeignMode).\n- A foreign file at the sidecar path is never overwritten or deleted\n  (TestSidecarIsNeverClobbered, TestRemoveLeavesForeignSidecarAlone).\n- A planted symlink at a predictable temp name is not followed\n  (TestAtomicWriteDoesNotFollowAPlantedTempSymlink; keep the Go test's\n  `pre-commit.roast-tmp` name and add one for `.pre-commit.roast-*`).\n- `core.hooksPath` is honoured (TestHonorsCoreHooksPath).\n- Decision round trip including aliases, and recording a decision clears\n  the notice (TestDecisionRoundTrip, TestRecordDecisionClearsNotice).\n- Appendability table from 2.5 (TestAppendable): drive through `gate\n  enable` (appended vs untouched) or, if too slow, test `appendable`\n  directly as a pure function.\n- Enable refuses without a toplevel config (exit 2) and works with one\n  (TestGateEnableRefusesConfigTheHookCannotSee,\n  TestGateEnableWithToplevelConfig).\n\n**Shared dispatcher** (`core.hooksPath` pointing at a directory used by two\nrepos):\n\n- A shared hook does not review in a repo without local consent, even with\n  a global `roast.gate=enabled` (TestSharedGateRequiresLocalConsent).\n- Enrollment aliases agree between `readDecision` and the script\n  (TestGateEnrollmentAliasesMatchDispatcher).\n- Bootstrap does not adopt an inherited gate; refreshes a declined repo's\n  stale legacy dispatcher (TestBootstrapDoesNotAdoptInheritedGate,\n  TestBootstrapRefreshesDeclinedLegacyDispatcher).\n- Disable preserves the dispatcher for the other repo, refreshes a legacy\n  one, never touches a foreign sidecar\n  (TestSharedGateDisablePreservesOtherRepository,\n  TestSharedGateDisableRefreshesLegacyDispatchers,\n  TestSharedGateDisableNeverTouchesForeignSidecar,\n  TestGateCommandsKeepSharedDispatcher).\n\n**Bootstrap** -- CLI seam: `run(['review', ...])` against the fake\ninference server (approved config), with `interactiveTerminals` simulated\nand stdin answers supplied; assert `roast.gate`, `roast.gate-notice`, and\nhook presence:\n\n- A declined prompt is remembered and never re-asked\n  (TestBootstrapPromptDeclineIsRemembered).\n- Accepting installs and records `enabled`\n  (TestBootstrapPromptAcceptsAndInstalls).\n- Non-interactive runs hint once (`roast.gate-notice=sent`, no hook)\n  (TestBootstrapNonInteractiveHintsOnce).\n- `GIT_INDEX_FILE` set suppresses it (TestBootstrapSuppressesInsideHook).\n- `gate.offer: false` never prompts or hints, and does not consume the\n  notice (TestBootstrapNoOfferNeverPrompts,\n  TestGateOfferFalseStopsTheGateOffer).\n- `ROAST_NO_HOOK` has no effect (TestBootstrapIgnoresNoHookEnvironment,\n  TestNoHookEnvironmentDoesNotStopTheGateOffer).\n- No offer when the config is only in a subdirectory; offer with a\n  toplevel config, also under `--format json`\n  (TestReviewDoesNotOfferGateTheHookCannotRun,\n  TestReviewOffersGateWithToplevelConfig). Observe via\n  `roast.gate-notice`, not stderr text.\n\n**Gate settings** -- CLI seam:\n\n- Values come from the config, severity uppercased, env ignored\n  (TestGateSettingsComeFromTheProjectConfig).\n- Defaults 180 / HIGH (TestGateSettingsDefaultWhenUnset).\n- No config -> exit 2 (TestGateSettingsWithoutProjectConfigIsAUsageError).\n- Invalid `severity`, negative `timeout_seconds`, non-boolean `offer` ->\n  exit 2 (TestInvalidGateSettingsAreRejected).\n\n**Hook execution** -- real `git commit` in a temp repo (spawned with\n`execFile`), with a POSIX shell stub written at\n`<repo>/node_modules/.bin/roast` (mode 0755). The stub answers `gate\nsettings` from `STUB_TIMEOUT` / `STUB_SEVERITY` (optionally\n`STUB_SETTINGS_EXIT`, `STUB_SETTINGS_STDERR`); for any other call it\nappends `ARGS: $*`, the `git diff --cached --name-only HEAD` names, and the\nfull `git diff --cached HEAD` to `$STUB_LOG`, then optionally sleeps\n(`STUB_SLEEP`), prints `STUB_STDOUT` / `STUB_STDERR`, and exits\n`STUB_EXIT`. An empty log means no review ran. The seeded repo has `a.txt`\nstaged but not committed and `b.txt` committed by path (`git commit b.txt\n-m ...`), with `roast.gate=enabled`. Port the stub verbatim. Assert commit\nsuccess/failure and the log; where output must be checked, check for a\ntest-controlled marker the stub printed, not the script's own wording.\n\n- Path-scoped commit reviews only `b.txt`'s content\n  (TestGateReviewsOnlyThePathScopedCommitsContent).\n- Exit 1 blocks and the stub's stderr reaches the user\n  (TestGateBlocksOnFindingsAndPrintsThemToStderr).\n- `ROAST_SKIP=1` skips without running the stub\n  (TestGateSkipBypassesEntirely).\n- Empty stdout allows (TestGateTreatsEmptyStdoutAsInfrastructureFailure).\n- Other exits allow, including exit 2 for an untrusted config whose stderr\n  reaches the user (TestGateAllowsCommitOnOperationalFailure,\n  TestGateAllowsCommitWhenConfigIsUntrusted).\n- Missing binary allows (TestGateAllowsCommitWhenRoastIsMissing).\n- Timeout allows (TestGateTimesOutWithoutBlocking; sleeps, so gate behind\n  an opt-out env for quick runs); timeout and severity come from `gate\n  settings`, not env (TestGateTimeoutComesFromTheProjectRoast,\n  TestGateSeverityComesFromTheProjectRoast); a failing `gate settings`\n  allows (TestGateAllowsCommitWhenSettingsAreUnavailable).\n- Appended block runs alongside a foreign hook, including one that exits\n  early, and a non-executable hook does not run\n  (TestGateRunsAlongsideAForeignHook,\n  TestGateRunsInAForeignHookThatExitsEarly,\n  TestGateDoesNotRunWhenHookIsNotExecutable).\n\nSince the script is unchanged, these tests mainly prove the TS install\npath writes a working hook; they need `sh` and `git` only, no Node build.\n\n**ignore** -- CLI seam (`run(['ignore'])`, `run(['init', ...])`):\n\n- Creates `.gitignore` containing `/.roast/\\n`\n  (TestIgnoreCreatesToplevelGitignore).\n- Appends, adding a newline to an unterminated last line\n  (TestIgnoreAppendsToExistingGitignore).\n- Leaves each equivalent entry form unchanged\n  (TestIgnoreLeavesEquivalentEntryUnchanged).\n- Second run is a no-op (TestIgnoreTwiceIsIdempotent).\n- Outside a repository -> exit 2\n  (TestIgnoreOutsideGitRepositoryIsUsageError).\n- `init` adds the entry (TestInitIgnoresTheStateDirectory).\n\n## 6. Go baseline references\n\nAt commit `cd08f10`:\n\n- `internal/gate/gate.go`, `hook.go`, `bootstrap.go`, `pre-commit.sh`\n- `internal/cli/gate.go`, `internal/cli/ignore.go`\n- `internal/cli/cli.go` (`gateBootstrapCommands`, `PersistentPreRunE`,\n  `maybeBootstrapGate`, exit codes)\n- `internal/cli/config.go` (`gateConfigPath`, `errNoGateConfig`,\n  `loadProjectConfig`)\n- `internal/cli/prompt.go` (`promptYesDefault`)\n- `internal/cli/doctor.go` (`doctorGitChecks`, consumer)\n- `internal/cli/init.go` (consumer of `ensureStateIgnored`)\n- `internal/config/config.go` (`Gate`, `Offers`, `validateSettings`,\n  `Find`)\n- Tests: `internal/gate/hook_test.go`, `hook_exec_test.go`,\n  `bootstrap_test.go`, `shared_test.go`; `internal/cli/gate_test.go`,\n  `gate_config_test.go`, `ignore_test.go`, `settings_test.go` (gate\n  tests), `init_test.go` (`TestInitIgnoresTheStateDirectory`)\n\n## 7. Resolved\n\nResolved (maintainer decisions, see spec.md):\n\n1. Go's em dashes in status and error strings are kept as U+2014 in\n   output, written as `\\u2014` escapes in TS source (spec.md cross-cutting\n   \"Output strings\"); `pre-commit.sh` bytes are unchanged.\n2. A global `core.hooksPath` affecting `gate disable` stays as Go parity\n   (spec.md Further Notes).\n3. A one-line hook with no trailing newline gets a newline before Roast's\n   block is appended (spec.md change 19).\n4. The bootstrap prompt uses the one shared stdin reader.\n","numLines":789,"startLine":1,"totalLines":789}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FFM6WwBtpht95fLwUBzzXN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
