{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChB1xy17dJgC8ZDpXhcih","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run test:ts` pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\nTicket 29 is finished, and every checklist item has passing tests. `npx roast gate enable`, `gate disable` and `gate status` now work in the TypeScript CLI, and so does `npx roast ignore`. `npm run test:ts` passed 1967 of 1967, `npm test` (Go and launcher tests) passed, and the Go build passed. I made one more commit after that full run: it turns the em dashes back into `\\u2014` escapes in `src/gate/hook.ts`, because the editor tool had written them as literal characters. The strings are the same at runtime, and afterwards I reran the gate CLI tests, typecheck and lint, which all passed.\n\n**What was built**\n- **`src/gate/`** is a direct port of `hook.go`. The hook script is `internal/gate/pre-commit.sh` loaded byte for byte, so hooks the Go version installed are not reported stale. Hook files are read and written as raw bytes, so removing Roast's block from someone else's hook leaves the rest of the file unchanged. A one-line hook with no trailing newline gets one before the block (deliberate change 19).\n- **`src/cli/gate.ts`** adds `enable`, `disable` and `status` alongside the existing `settings`.\n- **`src/cli/ignore.ts`** adds `ignore` and exports `ensureStateIgnored` for `init` (ticket 34). There is no run-records module yet, so the `.roast` directory name is a private constant in this file for now.\n- **`writeFileAtomic`** needed no changes: it already had the final-mode option and the `.<basename>.roast-<random>` temp name with exclusive create.\n\n**How I tested it**\n- Most tests run the CLI in-process. Decisions and the `appendable` table are tested directly. The hook itself is tested with a real `git commit` against the ported shell stub.\n- After the first failing test I wrote the whole port in one step, since the Go code is the reference. So most later tests passed as soon as they were written, rather than failing first. To show they can still fail, I broke the code on purpose in seven places: the change-19 newline, the start-of-file ownership check, the requirement that a block contains the call line, refusing to overwrite a foreign sidecar, strict UTF-8 decoding, the `1` alias, and the shared branch of `remove`. Each break made tests fail.\n- The \"global `roast.gate=enabled`\" case conflicts with keeping `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null` for every git call. I set the non-local value through `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`/`KEY_0`/`VALUE_0` instead, and the hook's `--local` read correctly ignores it.\n- The two timeout tests sleep. Setting `ROAST_TEST_SKIP_GATE_TIMEOUT=1` skips them.\n\nI added the gate test helpers and these conventions to AGENTS.md. The per-ticket details are in `.redeye/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":397,"cache_read_input_tokens":193107,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":397},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"776ac9e1-0ccd-4600-8cd0-2b17f1742875","uuid":"96f395b1-a483-4fd3-95d3-48499c82d841","timestamp":"2026-11-18T20:23:08.507Z","request_id":"req_011ChB1xxiW4QzdosQRd2uBc"}
{"duration_api_ms":459527,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"776ac9e1-0ccd-4600-8cd0-2b17f1742875","total_cost_usd":4.211889800000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":110,"cache_creation_input_tokens":181772,"cache_read_input_tokens":8090169,"output_tokens":56962,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6926},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":181772,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1218,"cache_read_input_tokens":193107,"cache_creation_input_tokens":397,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":397},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":110,"outputTokens":56962,"cacheReadInputTokens":8090169,"cacheCreationInputTokens":181772,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":4.211889800000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":6926,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":181772,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_011k5kjd9eDuHTKrtWV4W3p5","tool_input":{"command":"cat >> test/cli/gate.ts <<'EOF'\n\nconst BEGIN = '# >>> roast pre-commit gate (managed by `roast gate`) >>>'\nconst END = '# <<< roast pre-commit gate <<<'\nconst INVOKE = '\"$(git rev-parse --git-path hooks/roast-pre-commit)\" || exit $?'\n\ntest('gate enable refreshes a stale own hook and a lost execute bit',\n    async t => {\n        const r = gateRepo(t)\n        writeHook(r.hook, '#!/bin/sh\\n# roast-gate-hook: v1\\n# old\\n')\n        let res = await gate(r, 'enable')\n        t.equal(res.code, 0, 'exits 0')\n        t.equal(read(r.hook), SCRIPT, 'stale content rewritten')\n\n        fs.chmodSync(r.hook, 0o644)\n        res = await gate(r, 'enable')\n        t.equal(res.code, 0, 'exits 0')\n        t.equal(modeOf(r.hook), 0o755, 'execute bit repaired')\n        t.equal(read(r.hook), SCRIPT, 'content unchanged')\n    })\n\ntest('gate enable appends to a foreign shell hook with a sidecar',\n    async t => {\n        const r = gateRepo(t)\n        const foreign = '#!/bin/sh\\nmake lint\\n'\n        writeHook(r.hook, foreign, 0o755)\n        const res = await gate(r, 'enable')\n        t.equal(res.code, 0, `exits 0 ${res.stderr}`)\n        const body = read(r.hook)\n        const lines = body.split('\\n')\n        t.equal(lines[0], '#!/bin/sh', 'shebang first')\n        t.equal(lines[2], BEGIN, 'block right after the shebang')\n        t.ok(lines.includes(INVOKE), 'block runs the sidecar')\n        t.ok(body.endsWith(`${END}\\nmake lint\\n`), 'their lines follow')\n        t.equal(read(r.sidecar), SCRIPT, 'sidecar is the script')\n        t.equal(modeOf(r.sidecar), 0o755, 'sidecar executable')\n        t.equal(localConfig(r, 'roast.gate'), 'enabled', 'consent')\n\n        // A stale sidecar is refreshed on the next enable.\n        writeHook(r.sidecar, '#!/bin/sh\\n# roast-gate-hook: v1\\n# old\\n')\n        const again = await gate(r, 'enable')\n        t.equal(again.code, 0, 'exits 0')\n        t.equal(read(r.sidecar), SCRIPT, 'stale sidecar refreshed')\n        t.equal(read(r.hook), body, 'hook not appended twice')\n    })\n\ntest('appending preserves the foreign hook mode', async t => {\n    for (const mode of [0o755, 0o750, 0o644]) {\n        const r = gateRepo(t)\n        writeHook(r.hook, '#!/bin/bash\\necho hi\\n', mode)\n        const res = await gate(r, 'enable')\n        t.equal(res.code, 0, 'exits 0')\n        t.ok(read(r.hook).includes(INVOKE), 'block appended')\n        t.equal(modeOf(r.hook), mode, `mode ${mode.toString(8)} kept`)\n    }\n})\n\ntest('a one-line hook without a newline gets one before the block',\n    async t => {\n        const r = gateRepo(t)\n        writeHook(r.hook, '#!/bin/sh')\n        const res = await gate(r, 'enable')\n        t.equal(res.code, 0, `exits 0 ${res.stderr}`)\n        const lines = read(r.hook).split('\\n')\n        t.equal(lines[0], '#!/bin/sh', 'the shebang line stands alone')\n        t.equal(lines[1], '', 'blank separator')\n        t.equal(lines[2], BEGIN, 'then the block')\n        t.equal(read(r.sidecar), SCRIPT, 'sidecar written')\n    })\n\ntest('non-shell and symlinked hooks are left untouched', async t => {\n    const r = gateRepo(t)\n    const python = '#!/usr/bin/env python3\\nprint(\"hi\")\\n'\n    writeHook(r.hook, python)\n    let res = await gate(r, 'enable')\n    t.equal(res.code, 0, 'manual enable exits 0')\n    t.equal(read(r.hook), python, 'non-shell hook byte-identical')\n    t.equal(localConfig(r, 'roast.gate'), 'enabled', 'consent recorded')\n    t.equal(read(r.sidecar), SCRIPT, 'sidecar for the manual line')\n\n    const s = gateRepo(t)\n    const target = path.join(scratch(t), 'husky-hook')\n    const shell = '#!/bin/sh\\nnpx lint-staged\\n'\n    writeHook(target, shell)\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(s.hook), { recursive:true })\n    fs.symlinkSync(target, s.hook)\n    res = await gate(s, 'enable')\n    t.equal(res.code, 0, 'symlinked enable exits 0')\n    t.ok(fs.lstatSync(s.hook).isSymbolicLink(), 'still a symlink')\n    t.equal(fs.readlinkSync(s.hook), target, 'same link target')\n    t.equal(read(target), shell, 'target untouched')\n    t.equal(localConfig(s, 'roast.gate'), 'enabled', 'consent recorded')\n})\n\ntest('gate disable removes only what Roast wrote', async t => {\n    // Own hook: deleted.\n    const own = gateRepo(t)\n    await gate(own, 'enable')\n    let res = await gate(own, 'disable')\n    t.equal(res.code, 0, 'exits 0')\n    t.ok(!fs.existsSync(own.hook), 'own hook deleted')\n    t.equal(localConfig(own, 'roast.gate'), 'declined', 'records declined')\n\n    // Appended: only the block goes, and the sidecar with it.\n    const app = gateRepo(t)\n    const foreign = '#!/bin/sh\\r\\n# theirs\\nmake lint\\nexit 0'\n    writeHook(app.hook, foreign, 0o750)\n    await gate(app, 'enable')\n    res = await gate(app, 'disable')\n    t.equal(res.code, 0, 'exits 0')\n    t.equal(read(app.hook), foreign, 'remainder byte-identical')\n    t.equal(modeOf(app.hook), 0o750, 'mode kept')\n    t.ok(!fs.existsSync(app.sidecar), 'owned sidecar removed')\n\n    // Untouched foreign hook: left alone.\n    const other = gateRepo(t)\n    writeHook(other.hook, '#!/bin/sh\\nmake lint\\n')\n    res = await gate(other, 'disable')\n    t.equal(res.code, 0, 'exits 0')\n    t.equal(read(other.hook), '#!/bin/sh\\nmake lint\\n', 'foreign kept')\n    t.equal(localConfig(other, 'roast.gate'), 'declined', 'declined')\n})\n\ntest('ownership is anchored', async t => {\n    const cases = {\n        'marker text mid-file':\n            '#!/bin/sh\\necho \"#!/bin/sh\"\\n# roast-gate-hook: v1\\nmake\\n',\n        'begin without end':\n            `#!/bin/sh\\n${BEGIN}\\n${INVOKE}\\nmake lint\\n`,\n        'marker pair without invocation':\n            `#!/bin/sh\\n${BEGIN}\\n# gone\\n${END}\\nmake lint\\n`,\n    }\n    for (const [name, body] of Object.entries(cases)) {\n        const r = gateRepo(t)\n        writeHook(r.hook, body)\n        const res = await gate(r, 'disable')\n        t.equal(res.code, 0, `${name}: disable exits 0`)\n        t.equal(read(r.hook), body, `${name}: never stripped or deleted`)\n    }\n})\n\ntest('a foreign file at the sidecar path is never clobbered', async t => {\n    const r = gateRepo(t)\n    const theirs = '#!/bin/sh\\n# their own roast-pre-commit\\n'\n    writeHook(r.sidecar, theirs)\n    writeHook(r.hook, '#!/bin/sh\\nmake lint\\n')\n    const res = await gate(r, 'enable')\n    t.equal(res.code, 4, 'enable fails rather than overwrite')\n    t.equal(read(r.sidecar), theirs, 'sidecar untouched by enable')\n    t.equal(read(r.hook), '#!/bin/sh\\nmake lint\\n', 'hook untouched')\n\n    const off = await gate(r, 'disable')\n    t.equal(off.code, 0, 'disable exits 0')\n    t.equal(read(r.sidecar), theirs, 'sidecar untouched by disable')\n})\n\ntest('hook writes do not follow planted temp symlinks', async t => {\n    const r = gateRepo(t)\n    git(r.dir, r.env, 'config', 'core.hooksPath', '.githooks')\n    const hooks = path.join(r.dir, '.githooks')\n    fs.mkdirSync(hooks)\n    const victim = path.join(scratch(t), 'precious')\n    fs.writeFileSync(victim, 'do not touch\\n')\n    fs.symlinkSync(victim, path.join(hooks, 'pre-commit.roast-tmp'))\n    for (let i = 0; i < 16; i++) {\n        fs.symlinkSync(victim,\n            path.join(hooks, `.pre-commit.roast-${i.toString(16)}`))\n    }\n    const res = await gate(r, 'enable')\n    t.equal(res.code, 0, `exits 0 ${res.stderr}`)\n    t.equal(read(victim), 'do not touch\\n', 'victim untouched')\n    t.equal(read(path.join(hooks, 'pre-commit')), SCRIPT, 'hook written')\n})\n\ntest('core.hooksPath is honoured', async t => {\n    const r = gateRepo(t)\n    git(r.dir, r.env, 'config', 'core.hooksPath', 'custom-hooks')\n    const res = await gate(r, 'enable')\n    t.equal(res.code, 0, 'exits 0')\n    t.equal(read(path.join(r.dir, 'custom-hooks', 'pre-commit')), SCRIPT,\n        'hook written under core.hooksPath')\n    t.ok(!fs.existsSync(r.hook), 'not in .git/hooks')\n})\n\ntest('gate status prints three lines and never mutates', async t => {\n    const r = gateRepo(t)\n    for (const step of [[], ['enable'], ['disable']]) {\n        if (step.length) await gate(r, ...step)\n        const before = localConfig(r, 'roast.gate')\n        const res = await gate(r, 'status')\n        t.equal(res.code, 0, 'exits 0')\n        t.equal(res.stdout.trimEnd().split('\\n').length, 3, 'three lines')\n        t.equal(localConfig(r, 'roast.gate'), before, 'no decision change')\n    }\n})\n\ntest('gate subcommand arguments', async t => {\n    const r = gateRepo(t)\n    for (const sub of ['enable', 'disable', 'status']) {\n        const res = await gate(r, sub, 'extra')\n        t.equal(res.code, 2, `${sub} with an extra argument exits 2`)\n    }\n    t.ok(!fs.existsSync(r.hook), 'nothing installed')\n    const bare = await gate(r)\n    t.equal(bare.code, 0, 'bare gate exits 0')\n    const outside = scratch(t)\n    for (const sub of ['enable', 'disable', 'status']) {\n        const res = await runRoast(['gate', sub],\n            { cwd:outside, env:r.env })\n        t.equal(res.code, 2, `${sub} outside a repository exits 2`)\n    }\n})\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='test/cli/gate.ts'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"import {\n    gateRepo,\n    localConfig,\n    modeOf,\n    read,\n    type GateRepo,\n} from '../gate/helpers.js'\"\"\",\"\"\"import {\n    gateRepo,\n    git,\n    localConfig,\n    modeOf,\n    read,\n    scratch,\n    writeHook,\n    type GateRepo,\n} from '../gate/helpers.js'\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode .redeye/one.ts test/cli/gate.ts 2>&1 | grep -v \"^ok\" | tail -30"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Unfx59Tn5QQr8MJFkkrNyH","tool_input":{"command":"cat > src/cli/ignore.ts <<'EOF'\n// `roast ignore` (spec 12, 2.13): adds the run-record state directory to\n// the toplevel .gitignore. `init` reuses ensureStateIgnored.\nimport fs from 'node:fs/promises'\nimport path from 'node:path'\nimport { gitRoot } from '../git/git.js'\nimport type { CommandArgs, CommandDef, RunContext } from './command.js'\nimport { UsageError } from './errors.js'\n\n// Roast's project-local state directory at the Git toplevel.\nconst STATE_DIR = '.roast'\n\nexport const STATE_IGNORE_ENTRY = `/${STATE_DIR}/`\n\n// Lines that already ignore the toplevel state directory.\nconst EQUIVALENT = new Set([\n    `/${STATE_DIR}/`, `/${STATE_DIR}`, `${STATE_DIR}/`, STATE_DIR,\n])\n\nfunction fail (text:string, err:unknown):Error {\n    const msg = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)\n    return new Error(`${text}: ${msg}`, { cause:err })\n}\n\n// Appends STATE_IGNORE_ENTRY to <repo>/.gitignore unless an equivalent\n// line is present, creating the file and terminating an unterminated last\n// line first. Reports the path and whether the file changed.\nexport async function ensureStateIgnored (\n    repo:string\n):Promise<{ path:string, added:boolean }> {\n    const file = path.join(repo, '.gitignore')\n    let data = Buffer.alloc(0)\n    try {\n        data = await fs.readFile(file)\n    } catch (err) {\n        if ((err as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code !== 'ENOENT') {\n            throw fail(`read ${file}`, err)\n        }\n    }\n    const lines = data.toString('utf8').split('\\n')\n    if (lines.some(line => EQUIVALENT.has(line.trim()))) {\n        return { path:file, added:false }\n    }\n    let addition = `${STATE_IGNORE_ENTRY}\\n`\n    if (data.length > 0 && data[data.length - 1] !== 0x0a) {\n        addition = '\\n' + addition\n    }\n    let handle:fs.FileHandle\n    try {\n        handle = await fs.open(file, 'a', 0o644)\n    } catch (err) {\n        throw fail(`open ${file}`, err)\n    }\n    try {\n        await handle.write(addition)\n    } catch (err) {\n        await handle.close().catch(() => {})\n        throw fail(`append ${file}`, err)\n    }\n    try {\n        await handle.close()\n    } catch (err) {\n        throw fail(`close ${file}`, err)\n    }\n    return { path:file, added:true }\n}\n\nasync function ignoreHandler (\n    _args:CommandArgs,\n    ctx:RunContext\n):Promise<void> {\n    let repo:string\n    try {\n        repo = await gitRoot(ctx.cwd, {\n            env:ctx.env as NodeJS.ProcessEnv,\n            signal:ctx.signal,\n        })\n    } catch (err) {\n        if (ctx.signal.aborted) throw err\n        const msg = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)\n        throw new UsageError(msg, { cause:err })\n    }\n    const { path:file, added } = await ensureStateIgnored(repo)\n    ctx.stdout.write(added ?\n        `added ${STATE_IGNORE_ENTRY} to ${file}\\n` :\n        `${file} already ignores ${STATE_IGNORE_ENTRY}\\n`)\n}\n\nexport const ignoreCommand:CommandDef = {\n    command:'ignore',\n    describe:`Add ${STATE_IGNORE_ENTRY} to the toplevel .gitignore`,\n    handler:ignoreHandler,\n}\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/cli/commands.ts'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"import { gateCommand } from './gate.js'\\n\",\"import { gateCommand } from './gate.js'\\nimport { ignoreCommand } from './ignore.js'\\n\")\ns=s.replace(\"    gateCommand,\\n]\",\"    gateCommand,\\n    ignoreCommand,\\n]\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode .redeye/one.ts test/cli/ignore.ts 2>&1 | grep -E \"^not ok|^# (pass|fail)\""}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":62,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run test:ts` pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\nTicket 29 is finished, and every checklist item has passing tests. `npx roast gate enable`, `gate disable` and `gate status` now work in the TypeScript CLI, and so does `npx roast ignore`. `npm run test:ts` passed 1967 of 1967, `npm test` (Go and launcher tests) passed, and the Go build passed. I made one more commit after that full run: it turns the em dashes back into `\\u2014` escapes in `src/gate/hook.ts`, because the editor tool had written them as literal characters. The strings are the same at runtime, and afterwards I reran the gate CLI tests, typecheck and lint, which all passed.\n\n**What was built**\n- **`src/gate/`** is a direct port of `hook.go`. The hook script is `internal/gate/pre-commit.sh` loaded byte for byte, so hooks the Go version installed are not reported stale. Hook files are read and written as raw bytes, so removing Roast's block from someone else's hook leaves the rest of the file unchanged. A one-line hook with no trailing newline gets one before the block (deliberate change 19).\n- **`src/cli/gate.ts`** adds `enable`, `disable` and `status` alongside the existing `settings`.\n- **`src/cli/ignore.ts`** adds `ignore` and exports `ensureStateIgnored` for `init` (ticket 34). There is no run-records module yet, so the `.roast` directory name is a private constant in this file for now.\n- **`writeFileAtomic`** needed no changes: it already had the final-mode option and the `.<basename>.roast-<random>` temp name with exclusive create.\n\n**How I tested it**\n- Most tests run the CLI in-process. Decisions and the `appendable` table are tested directly. The hook itself is tested with a real `git commit` against the ported shell stub.\n- After the first failing test I wrote the whole port in one step, since the Go code is the reference. So most later tests passed as soon as they were written, rather than failing first. To show they can still fail, I broke the code on purpose in seven places: the change-19 newline, the start-of-file ownership check, the requirement that a block contains the call line, refusing to overwrite a foreign sidecar, strict UTF-8 decoding, the `1` alias, and the shared branch of `remove`. Each break made tests fail.\n- The \"global `roast.gate=enabled`\" case conflicts with keeping `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null` for every git call. I set the non-local value through `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`/`KEY_0`/`VALUE_0` instead, and the hook's `--local` read correctly ignores it.\n- The two timeout tests sleep. Setting `ROAST_TEST_SKIP_GATE_TIMEOUT=1` skips them.\n\nI added the gate test helpers and these conventions to AGENTS.md. The per-ticket details are in `.redeye/notes.md`, which is not committed.","ttft_ms":2151,"type":"result","duration_ms":806005,"uuid":"c56de4fd-9929-4b89-876f-4eb20531aef4","ttft_stream_ms":1687,"time_to_request_ms":146,"first_content_frame_ms":1689,"queued_tu